9292,stem-challenge-task-3-competition,"# Overview

**Watch a quick overview of this task:** [https://share.synthesia.io/1342366a-0f67-447a-9e70-365d1937dae7]

In the third task, your challenge is to identify and locate different aircraft types. 
----------------------
# Description

#### Mission Briefing: Identifying the Unknown

This task builds upon previous work by increasing the complexity of the dataset. Instead of identifying all objects as 'airplane,' you will distinguish between two aircraft classes. Your objective is to train and optimize a YOLOv11 model to accurately detect and classify these diverse objects.


#### The Challenge of Multi-Class Detection

In real-world airspace monitoring, it is not enough to detect objects - you must also distinguish between different types. This task mirrors real-world scenarios where AI systems must identify known aircraft and flag unauthorized intruders (like rogue aircrafts) to ensure safety and security.

#### Your Mission Objectives

1. Train a YOLOv11 model to identify and classify multiple aircraft types.
2. Adjust advanced hyperparameters (epochs, learning rate, input image size, etc.) for optimal performance.
3. Evaluate your model's accuracy in detecting and distinguish between different classes.
4. Submit your predictions for scoring and track your progress on the leaderboard.

----------------------
# Evaluation

Similar to task 1, the score will based on mAP@50.","# Dataset Description

### Overview

This dataset is designed for object detection of military aircraft and encompasses two (2) different military aircraft types.",False,True
