9295,itj-labs-fruit-classification-challenge,"# Overview

Welcome to the ITJ LABS Fruit Classification Challenge! ??????

In this competition, your goal is to develop an image classification model that can accurately identify 10 common fruits from images. This is a great opportunity to practice computer vision, deep learning, and convolutional neural networks (CNNs) while working with real-world image data.","# Dataset Description

This section describes the **files, structure, and format** of the dataset provided for the **ITJ LABS Fruit Classification Challenge**. Understanding this will help participants efficiently **train, validate, and test their models**.

## **?? Files Provided**
Participants will have access to the following files:

| File Name               | Description |
|-------------------------|-------------|
| `train_dataset.csv`     | Training set: Labeled images for model training. |
| `val_dataset.csv`       | Validation set: Labeled images for model tuning. |
| `test_dataset.csv`      | Test set: Unlabeled images for final evaluation. |
| `sample_submission.csv` | Example format for submission predictions. |
| `structured_fruit_dataset.zip` | Full dataset with images, structured into train, validation, and test folders. |

## **?? Dataset Structure**
The dataset is divided into **three subsets**:  

?? **Train** ¡ú 80% of the data, used for training.  
?? **Validation** ¡ú 10% of the data, used for tuning hyperparameters.  
?? **Test** ¡ú 10% of the data, used for generating predictions for submission.  

Each subset follows this structure:
```
structured_fruit_dataset/
 ©À©¤©¤ train/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Apple Red 1/
 ©¦     ©¦    ©À©¤©¤ img_01.jpg
 ©¦     ©¦    ©À©¤©¤ img_02.jpg
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Banana 1/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Grape Blue 1/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Kiwi 1/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Lemon 1/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Mango 1/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Orange 1/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Peach 1/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Pineapple 1/
 ©¦     ©À©¤©¤ Strawberry 1/
 ©¦
 ©À©¤©¤ val/    # Same structure as train
 ©À©¤©¤ test/   # Same structure but without labels
 ©À©¤©¤ train_dataset.csv
 ©À©¤©¤ val_dataset.csv
 ©À©¤©¤ test_dataset.csv
 ©À©¤©¤ sample_submission.csv
```

## **?? Data Format**
Each CSV file (`train_dataset.csv`, `val_dataset.csv`, `test_dataset.csv`) follows this structure:

| **File Name**       | **Label**       |
|--------------------|----------------|
| train/Apple Red 1/img_01.jpg | Apple Red 1  |
| train/Banana 1/img_02.jpg    | Banana 1     |
| train/Grape Blue 1/img_03.jpg | Grape Blue 1 |
| train/Kiwi 1/img_04.jpg      | Kiwi 1       |
| ...              | ...          |

### **1?? Train & Validation CSV**
- Each row contains an **image file path** and its **corresponding fruit label**.
- Labels belong to one of **10 fruit classes**.

### **2?? Test CSV**
- Contains **only image paths** (no labels).
- You need to predict the correct fruit class.

### **3?? Sample Submission CSV**
Your **submission file** must follow this structure:
| ID  | Outcome   |
|-----|----------|
| 0   | Apple Red  |
| 1   | Banana  |
| 2   | Grape Blue |
| ... | ... |

Each row corresponds to an **image ID** in the test set and the **predicted fruit class**.

## **?? Fruit Classes in the Dataset**
The dataset contains images from the following **10 fruit categories**:

| ID  | Fruit Class   |
|-----|-------------|
| 1??  | Apple Red  |
| 2??  | Banana  |
| 3??  | Grape Blue  |
| 4??  | Kiwi  |
| 5??  | Lemon  |
| 6??  | Mango  |
| 7??  | Orange  |
| 8??  | Peach  |
| 9??  | Pineapple  |
| ??  | Strawberry  |

## **?? Class Distribution**
Below is an example visualization of the number of images per class in the **training set**:

```python
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Load CSV
df = pd.read_csv(""train_dataset.csv"")

# Plot Class Distribution
plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))
df[""Label""].value_counts().plot(kind=""bar"", color=""skyblue"", edgecolor=""black"")
plt.title(""Class Distribution in Training Dataset"")
plt.xlabel(""Fruit Class"")
plt.ylabel(""Number of Images"")
plt.xticks(rotation=45)
plt.grid(axis=""y"", linestyle=""--"", alpha=0.7)
plt.show()
```

## **?? Important Notes**
- **Image format**: All images are **RGB (3-channel)**.
- **Image size**: **64x64 pixels** (preprocessed for efficiency).
- **Ensure correct file pathing**: Model training requires the correct directory structure.
- **Class names are case-sensitive**: Follow exact names as provided.

## **?? Need Help?**
If you have any questions about the dataset or encounter any issues, feel free to ask in the **discussion forum**! ??

?? **Now, download the dataset and start training your fruit classification model!** ??????",False,True
