9298,aiquest-bangla-sentiment-analysis-competition,"# Overview

# About aiquest
aiquest is a pioneering educational platform focused on making advanced technology education accessible in Bangla. With a mission to break language barriers in tech education, aiquest offers comprehensive live courses in Python, Data Science, Machine Learning, Deep Learning, Generative AI, Statistics, Data Analysis, Data Engineering, and Web Development¡ªall delivered in Bangla.

# Why Choose aiquest?
**Learn in Your Mother Tongue:** All courses are taught in Bangla, making complex technical concepts easier to understand.
**Live Interactive Sessions:** Engage directly with experienced instructors who provide real-time feedback.
**Practical Skill Development:** Hands-on projects and exercises that prepare you for real-world challenges.
**Community Support:** Join a growing community of Bangla-speaking tech enthusiasts and professionals.
**Career-Focused Curriculum:** Courses designed to meet industry demands and enhance employability.

# Our Impact
aiquest is transforming the tech education landscape in Bangladesh and Bengali-speaking regions by democratizing access to high-quality technical education. By removing language barriers, we're empowering the next generation of data scientists, AI specialists, and developers who might otherwise be excluded from the global tech revolution.

# Join the Movement
Whether you're a beginner looking to start your tech journey or a professional aiming to upskill, aiquest provides the perfect learning environment in a language you're comfortable with. Experience the difference between learning advanced technical skills in your mother tongue and becoming part of Bangladesh's growing tech ecosystem.
Experience the power of learning in your mother tongue - where complex technical concepts become clear and accessible. 
**Visit our** [Website:](https://aiquest.org/)
**Visit our** [Channel](https://youtube.com/studymart)

# Bangla Sentiment Analysis Challenge

## Goal
Develop a machine learning model that can accurately classify Bangla text as having positive, negative, or neutral sentiment.

This competition focuses on sentiment analysis for Bangla language text specifically related to banking and company services. Your task is to build a model that can understand the sentiment expressed in customer comments, reviews, and feedback.

## Recognition 
The top 5 performers will gain recognition, certificate, and visibility within the AIQuest community. Each will receive a fully-funded course from www.aiquest.org/courses.
----------------------
# Description

# About the Challenge

Sentiment analysis is a crucial component in understanding customer opinions and feedback. While this technology has advanced significantly for languages like English, Bangla - spoken by more than 230 million people worldwide - still lacks robust sentiment analysis resources.

## Dataset (Public)
The competition dataset consists of 100+ carefully curated Bangla text samples. 

## Dataset (Private)
Private dataset will be complex uncleaned and imbalanced do your best for handle the complex scenarios by your model. Best of luck.

Each entry contains:
- Text in Bangla related to banking and company services
- A sentiment label (positive, negative, or neutral)

The training data has been designed to cover various aspects of customer interactions, including:
- Service quality feedback
- Product reviews
- Customer support experiences
- General inquiries
- Feature requests

## Why This Matters

Accurate sentiment analysis in Bangla has numerous real-world applications:
- Helping companies understand customer satisfaction
- Improving product and service offerings based on feedback
- Monitoring brand perception on social media
- Enhancing customer support systems

## Submission Format

Participants must submit their predictions in CSV format as specified in the Evaluation section.
----------------------
# Evaluation

## Evaluation Metric

Submissions are evaluated using **macro F1-score**. This metric was chosen because:
1. It accounts for both precision and recall
2. The macro averaging gives equal weight to each class, which is important for our balanced dataset
3. It handles the multi-class nature of our problem (positive, negative, neutral)

## Submission File Format

For each ID in the test set, you must predict the sentiment class. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

id,sentiment
0,positive
1,negative
2,neutral
...

The 'sentiment' column must contain one of three values: 'positive', 'negative', or 'neutral'.",,True,True
