9330,pml-m4-makeup-hackathon,"# Overview

Hopkins is one of the great hospital systems of the world.
It is therefore fitting that we work with healthcare data.
The data (SUPPORT2) is hosted at the University of California, Irvine: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/880/support2.

Your purpose: 
* To develop and validate two properly-fitted classifiers to predict whether a patient will die in hospital (Target: hospdead). The two models you develop should be a) a logit model, and b) a Random Forest classifier. * Your performance metric is F1.
* To include a learning curve for both models to assess fit. Contrast the performance and fit of the two models. Notebooks that include models with appropriate feature selection, cross-validation, hyperparameter tuning and are well-fitted will earn higher grades.
