9338,predicting-social-media-performance,"# Overview

The goal of this competition is to predict the total number of social media interactions for different social media posts made by a renowned company.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F3745768%2Fbe3aa36e50f766b906c3f4424d1d88e4%2FUntitled.png?generation=1742146515926868&alt=media)
[Source of Image] (https://www.aamplify.marketing/blog/what-is-a-good-facebook-engagement-rate)

----------------------
# Description

The social media post interactions (sum of likes, shares, and comments) play a crucial role in determining the social media performance of a company and its brand reputation. Primarily, the count of social media interactions depends on several factors such as `Page total likes`,  `Type of post`, `Time of post`, and many others. With 15 explanatory variables describing (almost) every aspect of social media posts, this competition challenges you to predict their `Total Interactions' (Y).


----------------------
# Evaluation

## Goal

Your job is to predict the social media interactions for each instance for the test dataset (100 data points). For each observation in the test set, you must predict the value of the `Total Interactions` variable using 15 input variables.  

## Metric

Submissions are evaluated on R2 Score (coefficient of determination) between the observed number of interactions and the predicted value. 

You can download an example submission file (sample_submission.csv) on the Data page.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **Training_Data_Predictors.csv** - the training set predictors
*   **Train_Target.csv** - the training set target
*   **Test_Data_Predictors.csv** - the test set predictors
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
