9361,regresi-lab-6-regression,"# Overview

Kompetisi Kaggle Lab 6 ini menguji pemahaman mahasiswa mengenai implementasi penggunaan algoritma Linear Regression, Lasso Regression, dan Ridge Regression pada dataset yang sesuai.

Pada kompetisi kali ini mahasiswa dapat mencoba tiga dari lima jenis algoritma yang sedang berada dalam topik Lab 6 ini, yaitu model linear untuk kasus regresi (Linear Regression, Lasso Regression, dan Ridge Regression) serta memakai yang terbaik dari antara ketiga model tersebut.

Kompetisi ini juga bertujuan untuk menggali kreativitas mahasiswa dalam melakukan preprocessing pada dataset yang ada sehingga dapat dihasilkan hasil yang terbaik.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Dalam kompetisi ini, penilaian atas pengiriman peserta didasarkan pada nilai R squared (R^2) dari model regresi yang telah dibuat. R squared adalah metrik umum yang digunakan untuk mengevaluasi kinerja model regresi.","# Dataset Description

**Manufacturing Production Efficiency Metrics**

---

## Overview

This dataset provides a collection of records related to manufacturing or production processes across different departments and time periods. Each entry represents performance measurements on specific dates, along with details about operational parameters such as planned versus actual efficiency, work in progress, overtime, and more. It is suited for exploring trends in production efficiency, assessing the impact of workforce factors, and benchmarking planned versus real outcomes in a manufacturing environment.

---

## Column Descriptions

| Column Name         | Data Type   | Description |
|---------------------|-------------|-------------|
| **id**              | Numeric     | Unique identifier for each record. |
| **timestamp**       | Date/String | Date on which the record was captured (e.g., ""1/31/2015""). |
| **qtr**             | Categorical | The quarter indicator (e.g., Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5), which might represent a specific operational cycle or reporting period. |
| **dept**            | Categorical | Department code (e.g., A, B), which identifies the organizational unit or production line. |
| **weekday**         | Categorical | Day of the week on which the record was logged (e.g., Saturday, Monday). |
| **group**           | Numeric     | A grouping or shift indicator that could represent a team or work shift classification. |
| **planned_efficiency** | Numeric | The efficiency target set for the production process (e.g., 0.8 or 0.75). |
| **std_min_value**   | Numeric     | Standard minutes value; a benchmark or reference time measurement used for operational planning. |
| **work_in_progress**| Numeric     | Represents the volume or number of units in production that are yet to be completed; blank values indicate possible data omissions. |
| **extra_hours**     | Numeric     | The total extra hours worked beyond standard scheduling (e.g., overtime hours). |
| **bonus**           | Numeric     | Bonus values awarded, likely tied to performance or efficiency metrics. |
| **downtime**        | Numeric     | The duration (or cost) associated with downtime, indicating interruptions in production. |
| **inactive_workers**| Numeric     | Number of workers recorded as inactive during the period, possibly reflecting absenteeism or unutilized labor capacity. |
| **style_changes**   | Numeric     | Count of style or process changes implemented during the production period; these may influence efficiency. |
| **num_workers**     | Numeric     | The total number of workers active during the production period. |
| **real_efficiency** | Numeric     | The actual measured efficiency achieved during the period, which can be compared with the planned efficiency to gauge performance. |


## Files

*   **efficiency_train.csv** - the training set
*   **efficiency_test.csv** - the test set
*   **efficiency_sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
9362,ultimate-customer-churn-prediction-challenge,"# Overview

Customer churn is a major challenge for businesses, as losing customers directly impacts revenue and growth. In this competition, your goal is to build a machine learning model that can accurately predict which customers are likely to leave based on demographics, service usage, and feedback data.

By participating, you will gain hands-on experience with real-world customer analytics, improve your feature engineering and model evaluation skills, and compete to build the best-performing model! ??

?? Why This Matters?
Understand customer behavior using machine learning.
Help businesses improve customer retention strategies.
Work with structured, multi-source datasets just like in real-world AI projects.
?? Your Challenge
Train a model to predict customer churn using the provided datasets.
Optimize your model for F1-score to balance precision and recall.
Compete for the top spot on the leaderboard by improving your predictions!
This competition is designed to be a realistic and challenging experience, perfect for those looking to strengthen their data science and AI skills.
----------------------
# Description

Customer churn is a critical issue for businesses across industries. Losing customers can significantly impact revenue, making it essential for companies to predict and prevent churn. In this competition, you will develop a machine learning model to identify at-risk customers before they leave.

You will work with real-world structured datasets containing:

Customer demographics and subscription details
Service usage patterns and payment behavior
Customer satisfaction scores and complaint history
Your goal is to create a highly accurate predictive model that helps businesses retain customers by understanding key churn indicators. The competition will be judged based on the F1-score, ensuring that both false positives and false negatives are carefully balanced.

This challenge is an excellent opportunity to:
? Gain hands-on experience with real-world customer analytics
? Enhance your skills in data preprocessing, feature engineering, and model tuning
? Compete with fellow data enthusiasts to build the best AI-powered churn prediction model

Whether you're a beginner or an experienced data scientist, this competition will test your ability to clean data, select features, and optimize machine learning models to make impactful business predictions.


----------------------
# Evaluation

Your model will be evaluated based on the F1-score, a metric that balances precision (how many of the predicted churners are actual churners) and recall (how many actual churners were correctly identified).

Since customer churn is often an imbalanced problem, where the number of customers who leave is much smaller than those who stay, the F1-score ensures that both false positives and false negatives are considered.

?? Leaderboard Calculation
Your final score will be based on:

Public Leaderboard: 50% of the test data (visible during the competition).
Private Leaderboard: 50% of the test data (used for final ranking).
The participant with the highest F1-score on the private leaderboard wins the competition! ??

?? Important Notes:
You must not manually adjust test data before predictions.
Submissions must follow the correct output format (i.e., a CSV file with predictions).
The final model should be generalizable to new, unseen data.","# Dataset Description

This competition provides three separate datasets, each containing different aspects of customer behavior. These datasets must be merged using the Customer_ID column to create a complete view of each customer¡¯s profile.

?? Key Details:

Age, Gender, Location ¡ú Demographic data
Subscription_Type ¡ú Plan type (e.g., Basic, Premium)
Account_Age_Months ¡ú How long the customer has been subscribed
Monthly_Spending ¡ú How much they pay each month
Churn (Target Variable) ¡ú 1 if the customer left, 0 if they stayed

Total_Usage_Hours ¡ú Total service usage time
Support_Calls ¡ú Number of times the customer called support
Late_Payments ¡ú Number of late payments
Streaming_Usage (%) ¡ú Percentage of usage related to streaming services
Discount_Used (%) ¡ú Percentage of total payments made with discounts

Satisfaction_Score (1-10) ¡ú Customer¡¯s rating of satisfaction
Last_Interaction_Type ¡ú Last interaction with support (Positive or Negative)
Complaint_Tickets ¡ú Number of complaints filed by the customer
Promo_Opted_In (1/0) ¡ú Whether the customer has opted into promotional offers",False,True
