9366,placement-puzzle-crack-the-hiring-code,"# Overview

This competition challenges you to predict whether a student will secure a job placement based on academic performance, educational background, and other factors. The dataset includes high school and degree percentages, specialization, entrance test scores, work experience, and skill-based assessments. Competitors must develop machine learning models to uncover key patterns that influence hiring decisions. Can you build the ultimate placement predictor?

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F3745768%2Ffc7429f103e721f39b8e83f2a0830221%2FImage.webp?generation=1742556736290836&alt=media)

----------------------
# Description

Campus placements are a critical transition from academics to professional careers. Companies consider multiple factors, including academic performance, specialization, entrance test scores, and communication skills, to make hiring decisions. Understanding which attributes contribute the most to job placements can help students prepare better and assist institutions in refining their training programs.

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F3745768%2Fd62b6e89b5bc176b5b9ddf869c340d9c%2FImage_2.webp?generation=1742557061852817&alt=media)

# Objective
In this competition, your task is to build a machine learning model that predicts whether a student will be placed based on various academic and skill-related factors. Given details such as high school and degree percentages, specialization, entrance test performance, work experience, and soft skills assessments, can you accurately determine who will secure a job offer?

# Dataset Overview
The dataset consists of multiple features covering different aspects of a student's profile:

**Academic Performance:** High school (SSC), higher secondary (HSC), degree, and MBA percentages.
**Board & Stream Information:** SSC and HSC boards, HSC stream, and degree specialization.
**Entrance Exams & Scores:** Entrance test taken, entrance test percentile, and S-TEST score.
**Skills & Experience:** Work experience (years), communication marks, project work marks, and BOCA (Business Oral Communication Assessment) scores.

Your goal is to leverage this information to develop a predictive model that classifies students as placed or not placed.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The dataset is labeled as follows:

 **`Placed` : 0**
 **`Not Placed` : 1**

## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict the class label of the `Placement` variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    `ID`, `Placement` 
     1,       0
     2,       0
     3,       0
    etc.

Evaluation of the model will be done based on the [`f1_score`](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.f1_score.html).","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **Train_Features.csv** - the training set predictors
*   **Train_Target.csv** - the training set target
*   **Test_Features.csv** - the test set predictors
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format",False,True
