9393,the-3rd-mi-ga-ijcai-challenge-track-1,"# Overview

The Micro-gesture Analysis for Hidden Emotion Understanding (MiGA) challenge is planned as a continuous, annual event, and each year MiGA will include different (multiple) challenge tasks, with large-scale datasets with expanding size.

Body gestures are an important form to reveal people¡¯s emotions alongside facial expressions and speeches. For special occasions when people intend to control or hide their true feelings, e.g., for social etiquette or other reasons, body gestures are harder to control and thus the more revealing clues of actual feelings compared to the face and the voice. Micro-gestures (MG) are defined as a special category of body gestures that are indicative of humans¡¯ emotional status. Representative instances include scratching the head, touching the nose, and rubbing hands, which are not intended to be shown when communicating with others, but occur spontaneously due to e.g., felt stress or discomfort. The MGs differ from indicative gestures which are performed on purpose for facilitating communications, e.g., using gestures to assist verbal expressions during a discussion. Although research on general body gestures is prevailing, it is largely about human¡¯s macro body movement, lacking the finer level consideration such as the micro-gestures discussed above. As well the studies are mainly concerned with recognizing the movement performed expressively, and the link between gestures and hidden emotions is yet to be explored.

As the third year of MiGA, we plan to set three challenge tasks (Tracks): MG classification,  MG online recognition and Behavior based emotion recognition, and participating teams can choose to compete on one or more of them.

## Official website of the challenge:

https://cv-ac.github.io/MiGA2025/
