The dataset for the proposed challenge is available. The MiGA challenge is planned as a continuous annual event. This year¡¯s Track 2 will use the **SMG dataset**, published in IJCV 2023.

The Spontaneous Micro-Gesture (SMG) dataset consists of 3,692 samples across 17 micro-gesture (MG) classes. These MG clips are annotated from 40 long video sequences (each lasting 10¨C15 minutes), totaling 821,056 frames. The data was collected from 40 subjects who were asked to narrate both real and fake stories to elicit spontaneous emotional responses. SMG includes four modalities: RGB, 3D skeletal joints, depth, and silhouette, captured using Kinect.

In this competition, participants are allowed to use either the skeleton modality, the RGB modality, or both.

**[Details about SMG dataset](https://github.com/mikecheninoulu/SMG)**

**The training and validation sets (skeleton + RGB modality) of the SMG dataset will be released for the competition on April 5th.**",False,True
