# Submit source code

 The challenge has officially ended, please follow [these](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1I4YibglsqL-q8fJVuuqRcE-9P1mgGuW6W4dyJ-COw3E/edit?usp=sharing) instructions to submit your source code, deadline is **27 May**. Top-3 runners will present their work at IJCAI2025. You can submit papers to the MiGA3 [Workshop](https://cv-ac.github.io/MiGA2025/) as well.
----------------------
# Description

## **Track 3 (Behavior based emotion recognition) description**  
In this track, we conduct behavior based emotion recognition from long video sequences. Unlike most existing datasets for emotion recognition that involve acted or intentionally performed behaviors, this task focuses on recognizing hidden emotional states based on body behaviors directly from in-the-wild interview press. The data comes from tennis players during post-match press conferences, where subtle and involuntary body movements naturally occur. Using match outcome (win/loss) as a proxy for emotional state, the goal is to infer emotion based on the long behavioral sequences. This task presents unique challenges, including modeling behavior-emotion relationships under noisy conditions and mining relevant cues from complex and unstructured body movements. Both skeleton and RGB modalities are provided, and multi-modal solutions are encouraged.
----------------------
# Schedule

Important Dates (might slightly adjust later)

Mar. 30, 2025. Call for Challenge online. Registration starts.
Apr 05, 2025. Release of training data.
May 11, 2025. Release of testing data.
May 25, 2025. Final testing data and result submission. Registration ends.
May 30, 2025. Release of challenge results.
June 07, 2025. **Extended**. Paper submission deadline (workshop).
June 10, 2025. Notification to authors.
June 15, 2025. Camera-ready deadline.
August 16, 2025. MiGA IJCAI 2025 Workshop,Montreal, Canada & Guangzhou, China.
----------------------
# Phases

**Phase 1: Development (30 March - 11 May)**
Development phase: create models and submit them or directly submit results on validation data, feedback is provided on the validation set only. In this phase the training and validation data are released, leaderboard is calculated on the submitted validation data results. 
**Phase 2: Final (11 May - 16 May)**
Final phase: test your models on the testing data and submit to the new leaderboard. In this phase the testing data (without labels) is released, the new and final leaderboard is calculated on the submitted testing data results.

Data can be found [here](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/the-3rd-mi-ga-ijcai-challenge-track-3/data).
----------------------
# Evaluation

Training datasets and the testing dataset (without annotation released) are from iMiGUE. We deploy a cross-subject evaluation protocol by dividing the 72 subjects into a training group of 37 subjects and a testing group of 35 subjects. For the behavior based emotion recognition track, 245 long videos for training and 10 long videos for validation, and the remaining 104 videos from iMiGUE will be used for testing.

Behavior based emotion recognition track: We evaluate the submitted algorithms with a binary classification (win/lose) accuracy. The algorithm needs to predict the correct emotion state (positive/negative) corresponding to the match results (win/lose) of the tennis players based on their body behaviors during the interview press. Submissions will be ranked on the basis of the accuracy on the testing set.


Submission format for classification track. Participants must submit their predictions following **the sample format below (1: win, 0: lose)**. The results will be evaluated on the server and displayed on the ranking list in real-time. The organization team has the right to examine the participants' source code to ensure the reproducibility of the algorithms. The final results and ranking will be confirmed and announced by organizers.


## Submission File
Participants must submit their predictions in the a single .csv file. Instructions and sample submission files will be released with the data.

The file should contain a header  (video_id , label) with  and have the following format:

    video_id , label
    68,1
    172,0
    etc.


 <!--The phase 2 sample submission for the final testing phase (May 2nd to May 12th) can be found [here](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CdJAtN4r8HvEz0D6oaxYeE1o2wXGzqmx/view?usp=sharing).**
