    etc.",,False,True
9505,synthetic-2-real-object-detection-challenge-2,"# Overview

# Synthetic 2 Real Object Detection Challenge 2??

### ?? Challenge Summary  
Welcome to the **second edition** of the **Synthetic-to-Real Object Detection Challenge!** Your task is to train object detection models using **100% synthetic data**. This setup mirrors real-world AI applications, where models trained in **controlled environments** must generalize to messy, unpredictable reality.

Participants will train a model on **synthetic soup can images** generated in [Falcon](http://duality.ai/edu?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2), Duality AI¡¯s digital twin simulation software, and then test the model¡¯s performance on previously **unseen real-world images**. The twist? **You can boost your score by creating your own digital twin-based synthetic data with Falcon!** [Create an account here to start learning how.](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation?learnWelcome=true&sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2)   

**What¡¯s New in This Challenge?**
Unlike the previous edition, this challenge pushes users to explore data manipulation. A benefit of using synthetic data is that you can create and modify datasets to better train your model. Users will be provided one dataset here on Kaggle + given access to 4 extra datasets on FalconCloud, each with unique characteristics that can help or hurt the model's training, including but not limited to:

- **Varied environment features**
- **Multiple camera distances and viewpoints**
- **Lighting and occlusion differences**

Competitors can also follow [Exercise 2](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/ex2-objdetection-newtwin?sidebarMode=learn?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2) to create their own unique supplementary datasets. Top performers will mix, match, and augment these datasets to close the Sim2Real gap¡ªand build the most robust object detector possible.

**What's In it for you?**  
- **Win prizes**: Cash awards, Certificates and Shoutouts on platforms like LinkedIn and Hugging Face with a chance to feature on our competition blog.  
- **Master synthetic data**: Learn skills applicable to real-world AI deployment.  
- **Boost your portfolio**: Showcase your AI & ML skills in real-world object detection.
- **[Free Falcon EDU access](http://duality.ai/edu?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2)**: Hands-on experience with high-fidelity synthetic data generation tools.  
- **Stand out to recruiters**: Rank high on Kaggle, build credibility, and showcase your skills on LinkedIn, GitHub, and resumes.
- **[Network & grow](https://discord.com/invite/dualityfalconcommunity)**: Compete with fellow students, ML engineers, and researchers, collaborating on our Discord to answer questions and build connections.

So, how well can your model **detect objects in real-world images after training only on synthetic data**? Let¡¯s find out!   

---

### ?? **Objective**
- **Train on synthetic datasets**: Use a combination of our synthetic datasets or **[generate your own with Falcon](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/ex2-objdetection-newtwin?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2)**.  
- **Test on real-world images**: Detect a soup can in real-world images. 
- **Score using mAP@50**: Achieve the highest **mAP@50** (Mean Average Precision at IoU 0.5) score.   

---

### ?? **Why Synthetic Data?**
Synthetic data is **cost-effective, scalable, and bias-free** ¨C yet synthetic-trained models often fail in real-world conditions  (referred to as the Sim2Real gap). Since 2018 [Duality] (https://www.duality.ai/?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2) has been building tools and strategies that bridge this gap, and we¡¯re sharing them with you! 

[Check out our main simulation tool, FalconEditor, via any of the cloud-based simulations available on our page!](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2)

The skills you develop in this challenge apply to: 

- Autonomous robots 
- Industrial automation  
- AI-driven quality control  
- Augmented reality (AR) & Computer Vision applications
- And many more cutting-edge technologies!

**Featured Tool**: [Falcon Editor](http://duality.ai/edu?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2)  
- Free subscription tier available, Sign up [here](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/ex2-objdetection-newtwin?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_2)   
