9533,movie-revenue,"# Overview

This competition is an in-class competition for the course, ""Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning (Spring 2025)"", in Renmin University of China.

The competition is to predict the box office revenue for movies, based on various information about the movies, including cast, crew, genres, keywords, budget, overview, release date, runtime, languages, production companies, production countries, vote count, vote average, and etc.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [Root Mean Squared Logarithmic Error (RMSLE)] (https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/model_evaluation.html#mean-squared-log-error) between the predicted revenue and the actual revenue.

## Submission File
For each `id` in the test set, you must predict a value for the `revenue` variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

id,revenue
108942,42620000
1436502,42620000
21299,42620000
1341821,42620000
344615,42620000
......","# Dataset Description

The dataset consists of 19022 movies from the TMDB (The Movie Database), including details like titles, ratings, release dates, revenue, genres, and much more.

## Files

*   **movies_revenue_train.csv** - the training set
*   **movies_revenue_test.csv** - the test set
*   **movies_revenue_sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format

## Columns

*   `id` - id of the movie
*   `title` - title of the movie
*   `vote_count` - the count of votes for the movie
*   `vote_average` -  the average votes for the movie
*   `status` - status of the movie
*   `release_date` - release date of the movie
*   `revenue` - revenue of the movie, Target variable
*   `runtime` - duration of runtime of the movie
*   `adult` - if the movie is suitable only for adult audiences
*   `backdrop_path` - URL of the backdrop image for the movie
*   `budget` - budget of the movie
*   `homepage` - homepage of the movie
*   `original_language` - original language of the movie
*   `original_title` - original title of the movie
*   `overview` - overview of the movie
*   `popularity` -  popularity score of the movie
*   `poster_path` - location of the poster of the movie
*   `tagline` - tagline of the movie
*   `genres` - genres of the movie
*   `production_companies` - production companies of the movie
*   `production_countries` - production countries of the movie
*   `spoken_languages` - spoken languages of the movie
*   `keywords` - keywords of the movie
*   `cast` - cast of the movie
*   `crew` - crew of the movie",False,True
