9546,eliva-25-medical,"# Overview

Your goal is to develop a machine learning model that can accurately predict a person¡¯s chronological age based solely on an X-ray (RX) image of their hand.
----------------------
# Description

In this competition, you¡¯ll be working with medical imaging data to solve a  real-world problem: predicting a person¡¯s age from an X-ray image of their hand.
This task has significant applications in fields like pediatric medicine, forensic science, and anthropology.

## The dataset
You will be provided with:
	?	Two datasets of anonymized hand X-ray images
	?	A training dataset with a corresponding CSV file with age labels for each image (in months) and sex.
	?	A test set without labels for external evaluation.


## Your task
You need to develop a solution that can take the X-ray image (and optionally sex) as input and predict the age in months. 
The test set is from a completely different cohort, so the main goal of this challenge is to generalize to new data. 

----------------------
# Evaluation

Your model will be evaluated using the Mean Absolute Error (MAE) between predicted and actual ages on the test set.


## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a probability for the TARGET variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    id, boneage
    1.png , 147
    2.png , 46
    etc.","# Dataset Description



## Testing data
The test set of X-ray images is provided in the test folder. You can find .png files (gray scale 8 bit format).
In the same folder, you can find a test.csv file with the following format:
    id, male
    1.png , TRUE
    2.png , FALSE
    etc.

## Training data
For training, we suggest using [RSNA 2017 dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/kmader/rsna-bone-age). The dataset include 12611 images using same data format (.png files and .csv with annotated boneage and sex).",False,True
9547,sampling-assisted-pathloss-rm-prediction-t-2-i,"# Overview

