# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [Mean squared error  (MSE) regression loss](https://permetrics.readthedocs.io/en/latest/pages/regression/MSE.html) between the predicted and observed location. The following formula is used for evaluation.
$$\text{MSE}(y, \hat{y}) = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=0}^{N - 1} ( y_i  - \hat{y}_i )^2
$$



## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a probability for the xmin, xmax, ymin, ymax variables. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    ID,xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax
    Alabama_Chevrolet_Blazer_2001_0AB1234 - 00AB123_1_18AB166.jpg,0,0,0,0
    Alabama_Chevrolet_C-K-series_2005_Vintage Vehicle (VAB123)_11_VLV009.jpg,0,0,0,0
    Alabama_Chevrolet_Chevelle_2007_Vanity Plates_11_BIGBLOC.jpg,0,0,0,0
    etc.","# Dataset Description

