[3] D. P?udowski, F. Spinnato, P. Wilczy¨½ski, K. Kotowski, E. Ntagiou, R. Guidotti, and P. Biecek, ""MASCOTS: Model-Agnostic Symbolic COunterfactual explanations for Time Series"", ECML PKDD 2025. Available: https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.22389

[4] K. Kotowski, C. Haskamp, J. Andrzejewski, B. Ruszczak, J. Nalepa, D. Lakey, P. Collins, A. Kolmas, M. Bartesaghi, J. Martinez-Heras, and G. De Canio, ¡°European Space Agency Benchmark for Anomaly Detection in Satellite Telemetry,¡± arXiv:2406.17826, 2024. [Online]. Available: https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.17826

[5] B. Wang, Y. Yao, S. Shan, H. Li, B. Viswanath, H. Zheng, and B. Y. Zhao, ¡°Neural Cleanse: Identifying and mitigating backdoor attacks in neural networks,¡± in Proc. IEEE Symp. Security and Privacy (SP), San Francisco, CA, USA, May 2019, pp. 707¨C723. [Online]. Available: https://doi.org/10.1109/SP.2019.00031","# Dataset Description

## Clean Model

The **clean_model** folder contains the baseline NHiTS Model [1] (PyTorch format) trained exclusively on unpoisoned ESA-AD [2] Mission 1 telemetry (channels 44, 45, 46). It serve as the reference model before any adversarial manipulation. It is also available in the [Models tab](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/trojan-horse-hunt-in-space/models).
The model was trained using the same pipeline as detailed in the [Train Clean Model Notebook](https://www.kaggle.com/code/ramezashendy/clean-model-training-notebook).

## Models with trojans

The **poisoned_models** folder contains poisoned NHITS models [1] (PyTorch format) in which triggers should be discovered. The same models are available in the [Models tab](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/trojan-horse-hunt-in-space/models).

## Baseline training dataset

The **clean_train_data.csv** file contains several years of real sensor measurements from 3 channels (channel_44, channel_45, and channel_46) of a large spacecraft operated by the European Space Agency. This file was used to train the clean baseline model according to the procedures given in the [Clean Model Training notebook](https://www.kaggle.com/code/ramezashendy/clean-model-training). 

Clean_train_data.csv is a resampled ESA-Mission1 data of the [ESA-AD dataset](https://zenodo.org/records/12528696) [2].

## Sample submission

The **sample_submission.csv** file is a sample submission file in the correct format.


### References

[1] C. Challu, K. G. Olivares, B. N. Oreshkin, F. G. Ramirez, M. M. Canseco, and A. Dubrawski, ¡°NHITS: Neural Hierarchical Interpolation for Time Series Forecasting,¡± Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, vol. 37, no. 6, Art. no. 6, Jun. 2023, doi: 10.1609/aaai.v37i6.25854.

[2] K. Kotowski K, C. Haskamp, J. Andrzejewski, B. Ruszczak, J. Nalepa, D. Lakey, P. Collins, A. Kolmas, M. Bartesaghi, J. Martinez-Heras, G. De Canio, ¡°European Space Agency Benchmark for Anomaly Detection in Satellite Telemetry,¡± 2024, arXiv:2406.17826.",False,True
