9641,spring-2025-old-battery-prediction-challenge,"# Description

## Welcome to the second (and final) Kaggle competition this quarter! 

Congratulations, you are on this page because you have reached the submission stage of the competition.

Please make sure you read through the *Introduction to Battery Lifetime Prediction* and *Introduction to Data Science Competition II* slide decks on the Course Canvas, Module 6. 

Please use the same Kaggle username you used for the Data Science Competition I in HW#5, so we can ensure HW#7 credit is assigned to the correct person.

You are now given the usage data of 108 old batteries, where a ""remaining usage life (RUL)"" value, until when the batteries will retire, was labelled for each battery. Your task was to predict the RUL for 19 unknown old batteries based on their usage data.

## Enter the Competition
- *Kaggle Leaderboard*: submit your predicted RUL for 19 old batteries in the test dataset on Kaggle, your submission will be ranked by MAE ([mean absolute error](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error#:~:text=In%20statistics%2C%20mean%20absolute%20error,an%20alternative%20technique%20of%20measurement.)). Top 5 will be announced on Friday, December 2nd, 2022. 

## Deadline of submission on Kaggle: 
**11.59 pm PDT, Thursday, May 22nd, 2025 **

## Acknowledgements
Dr. Sun thank authors of [this paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-019-0356-8) for providing the dataset, and Dr. Steven Torrissi and Dr. Amalie Trewartha for notebook and data preparation.
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for Kaggle Leaderboard is the [mean absolute error](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error#:~:text=In%20statistics%2C%20mean%20absolute%20error,an%20alternative%20technique%20of%20measurement.) between predicted and the ground truth remaining useful lifetime (RUL) for the 19 batteries in the test dataset.

## What should I submit?
To enter the Kaggle Leaderboard: your submission file (.csv) should contain two columns: Cell ID and Predicted Remaining Useful Life","# Dataset Description

## Training and test dataset

Full training and test dataset can be found under Module 6 on our course Canvas. If you have problems accessing to the data, please contact Dr. Sun!

## Metadata files on Kaggle
- train_metadata.csv contains 108 Cell IDs, with a remaining useful life (prediction target) labeled for each battery.
- test_metadata.csv contains 19 Cell IDs
- submission_example.csv contains an example submission file in the correct format.

Please submit a csv file on Kaggle that contains two columns: 19 Cells IDs in the test dataset, and your predicted remaining useful life (RUL) for each battery.",False,True
