9651,iccv-mslr-2025-track-2,"# Overview

Welcome to the **1st Multimodal Isolated Italian Sign Language Recognition Challenge**! ??

[https://multimodal-sign-language-recognition.github.io/ICCV-2025/](https://multimodal-sign-language-recognition.github.io/ICCV-2025/)

In this competition, you'll develop models to recognize **isolated Italian Sign Language (LIS) gestures** using synchronized ?? **RGB video** and ?? **Radar Doppler (RDM)** data, captured from a 60GHz radar system.

Your goal? Build a classifier that accurately identifies 126 LIS gestures ¡ª 100 medical-domain words and 26 alphabet letters ¡ª using **multimodal inputs** from our brand new preliminary dataset: the **MultiMeDaLIS** dataset.

The top 5 teams will be invited to present at the **MSLR Workshop** at **ICCV 2025 in Honolulu, Hawai?i** ?????.

?? Show off your multimodal learning skills and help shape the future of inclusive AI communication systems!
----------------------
# Description

This competition is built around **MultiMeDaLIS**, a novel preliminary dataset that pairs visual and radar data to capture isolated Italian Sign Language gestures. Each of the 205 recorded sessions includes all 126 gesture classes, performed by a professional signer.

?? **What makes it special?**
- **Multimodal inputs**: RGB + Radar
- **Real-life gestures**: medical terms + alphabet letters
- **Challenging variation**: subtle hand shapes, motion dynamics, and timing
- **Radar data**: extracted from a 60GHz radar with 3 antennas in L-shape configuration

You're encouraged to explore fusion strategies ¡ª early, late, or attention-based ¡ª to combine these complementary modalities into powerful gesture recognition systems.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Your submissions will be evaluated based on **Top-1 Accuracy** across the 126 gesture classes.

The competition includes:
- ??? **Training Set**: 100 fully-labeled sessions
- ?? **Validation Set**: 35 sessions without labels (for real-time leaderboard)
- ?? **Test Set**: 70 sessions without labels (for final leaderboard)

?? You may submit up to 2 predictions per day on the validation leaderboard. Finalists must provide **code and model checkpoints** to ensure reproducibility.
----------------------
# Submission Format

Your submission should be a **CSV** file with the following format:
```python
id,Pred
0,23
1,78
¡­
```
?	*id*: ID of each sample
?	*Pred*: your predicted class ID for that sample (integer from 0 to 125)

Make sure your file includes **all samples** provided in the evaluation split. Only complete submissions will be scored. ?
----------------------
# Timeline (All deadlines are at 23:59 Anywhere on Earth (AoE))

?	?? **Competition Launch & Training Data Release**: May 18, 2025

?	?? **Validation Set Release**: May 18, 2025

?	?? **Test Set Release**: June 2, 2025

?	?? **Final Submission Deadline**: June 23, 2025

?	?? **Winners Announced**: June 24, 2025

?	?? **Paper Deadline**: July 3, 2025

?	?? **Workshop**: October 19¨C20, 2025 at ICCV 2025, Honolulu, Hawaii ??
----------------------
# Bibliography

If you use the dataset or participate in the challenge, please cite the following works:
