9692,bin-ego-360-challenge-classification,"# Overview

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F16342273%2F54806d6ca5c3298b740c930a9360103f%2FScreenshot%202025-05-30%20at%2013.49.19.png?generation=1748609376448475&alt=media)

> **Important Notice:**

> **Important Notice:**
> **New Final Submission Deadline????10 August 2025 (AOE)**
> We are delighted to let you know that the challenge deadline has been extended! Now you have more time to cook your good stuff! 

> Because the initial Kaggle competition could no longer be re?opened after its closing date, **a new competition page has been created to host the extended track**:
https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/bin-ego-360-challenge-classification-ext

> All rules, evaluation metrics, and prizes remain unchanged (with an additional prize of registration fee!); only the schedule has shifted, and you can submit via kaggle's sandbox. If you submitted to the first competition, simply re?upload your final model predictions here before the new deadline. ?


## Goal of the [BinEgo-360](https://x360dataset.github.io/BinEgo-360/#challenge) Challenge

What does it take for a model to understand a scene¡ªis it enough to see it? To hear it? Or is there more?

We present an exciting new challenge at the frontier of panoptic video understanding. The goal is to explore **multi-perspective learning**¡ªunderstanding how the fusion of diverse viewpoints and modalities, such as egocentric vision, 360¡ã third-person context, audio, and location cues, can lead to a more complete and holistic representation of complex scenes.

Join us in pushing the boundaries of multi-view learning. Your solution could help shape the future of perception in robotics, AR/VR, and human-centric video intelligence.


~~~~

>**This challenge is only for the ICCV 2025 BinEgo360 workshop and Challenge, and all the prizes will be issued at the workshop**

## Context

This challenge is part of the [BinEgo-360](https://x360dataset.github.io/BinEgo-360/#challenge) workshop. **Winners of the challenge will be invited to jointly write a paper about the workshop and challenge to be included in the ICCV proceedings.** The objective of this track is to predict the scene label (**classification**) for a given video clip, following the scene categories provided in the dataset. For more details about the dataset, tracks, timeline, and submission rules, please visit: https://x360dataset.github.io/BinEgo-360/#challenge.

We primarily incorporate two types of videos:

- **First-person (egocentric) video** captures the visual experience from the capturer's point of view. It includes direct observations of objects, hands, and interactions at close range, often reflecting the actor¡¯s focus and activity. The content is typically constrained by a limited field of view and may include frequent occlusions due to body movement or object handling.
- **360¡ã third-person video** provides an omnidirectional view of the environment from an external perspective. It records the full spatial layout and captures multiple agents within the scene. This perspective remains external to the actor, without access to internal states or viewpoint-specific information.




----------------------
# Prizes

### Awards & Prizes

To recognize outstanding solutions, we will award top-performing teams based on final leaderboard rankings.

**Total Prizes Available:** 3 winning spots

- **1st Place** ¨C Insta360 X5 panoramic camera + GPU Cloud Credit (worth ¡ê5-15k) on SCAN 
- **2nd Place** ¨C Amazon / Taobao vouchers + GPU Cloud Credit (worth ¡ê5-15k) on SCAN
- **3rd Place** ¨C Amazon / Taobao vouchers + GPU Cloud Credit (worth ¡ê5-15k) on SCAN


All awards are sponsored by **Insta360**, **SCAN**, and **Allsee Technologies**.

----------------------
# Description

In this track, participants are tasked with predicting the high-level **scene category** for each video clip. Each clip is annotated with a single ground-truth label (e.g., *indoor cafe*, *forest*, *subway*), reflecting the semantic context of the environment.

To solve this task, participants may leverage any subset or fusion of the following modalities provided in the dataset:

- **360¡ã panoramic video**: Omnidirectional video capturing the entire surrounding scene from a fixed location.
- **Third-person frontal video**: A narrow-field view extracted from the 360¡ã video, offering less distortion but limited spatial coverage.
- **Egocentric monocular and binocular videos**: First-person views recorded alongside the 360¡ã video, ranging from zero to multiple clips, spatially distributed within the 360¡ã video.
- **Spatial 6-channel audio (360¡ã video)**: Multichannel spatial audio captured along with the 360¡ã video, preserving directional sound information.
- **Spatial 2-channel audio (egocentric video)**: Stereo audio recorded from the egocentric cameras.
- **GPS and weather metadata**: Geolocation and environmental context associated with each video clip.
- **Scene-level textual descriptions**: High-level summaries of the scene. *(Not provided for the validation set.)*


The objective is to explore **multi-view, multi-modal learning** for semantic scene understanding. This setting encourages models that integrate spatial, temporal, auditory, and textual cues for robust classification across diverse real-world environments.


----------------------
# Evaluation

### Scoring with Top-K Accuracy

Top-K Accuracy can be used as a scoring function by measuring whether the correct scene label appears in the top **K** predictions for each video clip. This allows evaluation of both strict (Top-1) and more tolerant (Top-5, Top-10) classification performance.

For a given value of $ K $, the **Top-K Accuracy score** is calculated as:

$$
\text{Top-}K = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \mathbb{1}\left[y_i \in \hat{Y}_i^{(K)}\right]
$$

Where:

- $ N $: total number of video clips in the test set  
- $ y_i $: ground-truth label for the $ i $-th clip  
- $ \hat{Y}_i^{(K)} $: set of top $ K $ predicted labels for the $ i $-th clip  
- $ \mathbb{1}[\cdot] $: indicator binary function that returns 1 if the condition is true, 0 otherwise","# Dataset Description

The challenge uses our public dataset 360+x for training/validation, and a held-out test set for the evaluation. The full dataset can be fetched: [https://huggingface.co/datasets/quchenyuan/360x_dataset_HR](https://huggingface.co/datasets/quchenyuan/360x_dataset_HR)


![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F16342273%2F645b624e0405ed841981d6377c0e9498%2Fteaser_video.gif?generation=1748609310125434&alt=media)

Dataset Overview:
360+x captures real-world environments from four synchronised viewpoints (360¡ã panoramic, binocular egocentric, monocular egocentric, third-person front) together with 6-channel spatial audio, GPS, weather and text metadata. The dataset is designed to study how an embodied agent could perceive, localise actions and recognise scenes when immersed in a space, while also observing itself from an external vantage.",False,True
9693,st-4035-2025-assignment-1,"# Overview

**ST 4035 Assignment #1 ¨C Kaggle Competition **

A retail company wants to predict whether a customer is likely to churn (i.e., stop doing business) based on customer behavior and demographics. You are provided with a dataset containing 5,000 customer records and 20 input features. Your task is to build a classification model to predict the binary target variable Churn.
Tasks:
1.	Load the dataset and perform basic exploratory data analysis.
2.	Preprocess the data (handle categorical variables, scale features, manage missing values if any).
3.	Train a Logistic Regression model. You are not supposed to use any advanced techniques like regularization methods or any other classification methods.
4.	Get the predictions from the model for the test_data dataset and upload . 

----------------------
# Description

**Dataset Features:**
?	CustomerID: Unique identifier
?	Age, Gender, AnnualIncome
?	SpendingScore, YearsAsCustomer, NumProductsPurchased
?	WebsiteVisitsPerMonth, LastPurchaseAmount
?	TimeOnApp, TimeOnWebsite
?	CustomerSatisfaction, PreferredDevice
?	Region, IsPremiumMember
?	ReceivedPromotions, ClickedAds
?	ReturnedItems, UsedCoupons
?	FeedbackScore
?	Churn (Target: 1 = Churned, 0 = Retained)","# Dataset Description

