## ?? **Data Description**

Welcome to the competition! Below is a detailed description of the provided files and their formats to help you get started smoothly.

---

### ?? **Provided Files**

* **train.csv**
  ¡ú Contains the training data, including features and labels (`Air Quality`).
  You will use this file to train your predictive models.

* **test.csv**
  ¡ú Contains the test data **without labels**.
  You will generate predictions on this data and submit them in the required submission format.

* **sample\_submission.csv (or submission\_template.csv)**
  ¡ú A template showing the required format for submission files.

---

### ?? **File Format**

| File Name      | Description                             |
| -------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| train.csv      | Full training set with features + label |
| test.csv       | Test set with features only, no label   |
| submission.csv | Your submission file with predictions   |

---

### ?? **Column Details**

Most files share these columns:

| Column Name                      | Description                                                        |
| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| index / row\_id                  | Unique row identifier                                              |
| Temperature                      | Ambient temperature (¡ãC)                                           |
| Humidity                         | Relative humidity (%)                                              |
| PM2.5                            | Fine particulate matter concentration (¦Ìg/m3)                      |
| PM10                             | Coarse particulate matter concentration (¦Ìg/m3)                    |
| NO2                              | Nitrogen dioxide concentration (ppm)                               |
| SO2                              | Sulfur dioxide concentration (ppm)                                 |
| CO                               | Carbon monoxide concentration (ppm)                                |
| Proximity\_to\_Industrial\_Areas | Distance to the nearest industrial area (km)                       |
| Population\_Density              | Population density in the area (people/km2)                        |
| Air Quality                      | **Label** ¡ª air quality category (e.g., Good, Moderate, Unhealthy) |

---

