9704,aikc-course-2025-final-competition-2,"# Overview

In this competition, you are challenged to predict the genres of video games based on their metadata and visual content. Each game is represented by its title, description, and one in-game screenshot. Since a single game can belong to multiple genres (e.g., ¡°Action¡±, ¡°RPG¡±, ¡°Multiplayer¡±), this is a multi-label classification problem.

Participants are expected to develop multimodal models that combine both textual and visual features to accurately assign all relevant genres to each game.

**Goa**l: Build a model that predicts all applicable genres for each game using its title, description, and screenshot.

AI Knowledge Club Links: [tg](https://t.me/aiknowledgeclub), [youtube](https://www.youtube.com/@AIKnowledgeClub)
----------------------
# Evaluation

In this competition, your task is to predict one or more genres for each game in the test set. For each game ID, your prediction must be a single string containing the list of genres, separated by commas. This format should match how labels are provided in the train.csv file.

Submissions will be evaluated using the macro-averaged F1-score, which computes the F1-score independently for each genre and then takes the unweighted average across all genres.

This means that rare genres are treated equally to frequent ones, encouraging models that perform well across the full range of genre labels.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   train.csv ¨C the training set. Each row contains information about a video game, including its title, description, an image URL, and the list of genres (target labels).
*   test.csv ¨C the test set. Same format as train.csv, but without the genres field. Your task is to predict the genres for each game in this file.
*   sample_submission.csv ¨C a sample submission file in the correct format. Use this as a template for formatting your predictions.

## Format and Columns

*   ID ¨C a unique identifier for the game.
*   title ¨C the game's title (short text).
*   description ¨C a textual description of the game (can be multiple sentences).
*   image ¨C a URL pointing to a representative image (screenshot or cover) of the game.
*   genres ¨C (train only) a string of one or more genre labels, separated by commas. This is the multi-label target you need to predict.",False,True
9705,descubrir-senal-sonido-2025,"# Overview



Preview
Gradiente descendiente (15%), estaba en un parque de la ciudad y escuche un ruido constante. Entonces tom¨¦ mi celular y realice la grabaci¨®n del sonido, observando la siguiente gr¨¢fica.

 
Cualquier sonido cosenoidal  tiene la forma y_hat =a * cos(bx + c) +  d, nuestro error deber¨ªa ser LSE (Least Square Error) entonces nuestra funci¨®n de error se puede escribir como e(x) = (y - y_hat)^2. Ahora con la funci¨®n de error tenemos que derivar a,b,c y d=0 (Calcula el gradiente que son las derivadas parciales con respecto a a,b,c) y aplicar el algoritmo de gradiente descendiente (Considerando que el gradiente funciona solo con funciones convexas vamos a tomar la parte de la se?al convexa, para encontrar los par¨¢metros). 

**Goal:**  Cargue el archivo con la prediction e incluir en el github la solucion teorica

----------------------
# Description

Gradiente descendiente (15%), estaba en un parque de la ciudad y escuche un ruido constante. Entonces tom¨¦ mi celular y realice la grabaci¨®n del sonido, observando la siguiente gr¨¢fica.

 
Cualquier sonido cosenoidal  tiene la forma y_hat =a * cos(bx + c) +  d, nuestro error deber¨ªa ser LSE (Least Square Error) entonces nuestra funci¨®n de error se puede escribir como e(x) = (y - y_hat)^2. Ahora con la funci¨®n de error tenemos que derivar a,b,c y d=0 (Calcula el gradiente que son las derivadas parciales con respecto a a,b,c) y aplicar el algoritmo de gradiente descendiente (Considerando que el gradiente funciona solo con funciones convexas vamos a tomar la parte de la se?al convexa, para encontrar los par¨¢metros). 

**Goal:**  Cargue el archivo con la prediction e incluir en el github la solucion teorica


```
def y_predict(a,b,c,d,x):
    return a * math.cos(b*x + c) + d

lr = 0.05
n = len(x)
batch = 100
epochs = 3000
rsl = []
a = random.random()
b = random.random()
c = random.random()
d = 0
for i in range(epochs):
    a_gradiente = 0
    b_gradiente = 0
    c_gradiente = 0
    d_gradiente = 0
    e = 0
    for m in range(batch):
        ix = int(random.uniform(0,n))
        e +=  (y[ix] - y_predict(a,b,c,d,x[ix]))* (y[ix] - y_predict(a,b,c,d,x[ix]))
        a_gradiente += # * de/da
        b_gradiente += # * de/db
        c_gradiente += # * de/dc
        
    a = a - lr * a_gradiente/batch
    b = b - lr * b_gradiente/batch
    c = c - lr * c_gradiente/batch

    e = e/batch
    rsl.append([a,b,c,d,e])
    print(f""error:{e} period:{b} amplitude:{a} constant: {c} "")
```
Recuerden que el error es
$$ e = { y- a* cos(bx+c) } ^2$$

----------------------
# Evaluation

La evaluacion del problema utilizara el mae del archivo enviado

## Submission File
Cada identificador debe tener el valor de la prediccion :

   example_id,TARGET
    2,0
    5,0
    6,0
    etc.","# Dataset Description

Archivos son

