9732,ml-nomads-downscaling-laws-tiny-image-net,"# Overview

# MLNomads: Downscaling Laws 

Do ""scaling laws"" only go up? We don't think so. Welcome to MLNomads: Downscaling Laws - CIFAR10, where we explore the art of achieving maximum impact with minimal resources.

If you're fascinated by the fundamental principles of learning and tired of competitions dominated by sheer compute power, you've found your community. This series challenges you to:

- Master Small-Scale Pretraining: Train your models entirely from scratch. No transfer learning, no pre-existing weights.
- Embrace ""Cheap AI"": We encourage innovative, efficient solutions that don't require a supercomputer.
- Transparent Evaluation: Compete based on performance on the full, public test set. No surprises with a hidden holdout. Your model's true generalization from the training data is the key.
- This isn't just about leaderboards; it's about discovering novel ""downscaling laws"" ¨C principles that govern how to learn effectively when data and compute are constrained.

Ready to innovate on a different scale? Join MLNomads!
Link: [www.mlnomads.com/discord](www.mlnomads.com/discord)


----------------------
# Description

Just classify things bro
----------------------
# Evaluation

Accuracy is all you need","# Dataset Description

this is tiny-imagenet",False,True
