9739,data-set-structure,"# Overview

**Welcome to the 2024 Kaggle Playground Series!** Happy New Year! This is the 1st episode of Season 4. We plan to continue in the spirit of previous playgrounds, providing interesting and approachable datasets for our community to practice their machine learning skills, and anticipate a competition each month. 

**Your Goal:** For this Episode of the Series, your task is to predict whether a customer continues with their account or closes it (e.g., churns). Good luck!
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [area under the ROC curve](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic) between the predicted probability and the observed target.


## Submission File
For each `id` in the test set, you must predict the probability for the target variable `Exited`. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    id,Exited
    165034,0.9
    165035,0.1
    165036,0.5
    etc.",,False,True
9740,multi-instance-object-detection-challenge,"# Overview

# Multi-Instance Object Detection Challenge ??

## ?? Challenge Summary  
Welcome to the **third edition** of the **Synthetic-to-Real Object Detection Challenge!** 

Your objective is to **detect multiple instances of a soup can** in real-world images using models trained on **only the synthetic data** you generate in [FalconCloud](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/cca0bc47-265a-4f67-843f-a434b63271b3?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3), the cloud version of Duality AI¡¯s digital twin simulation software. All you need is a computer and internet access, and you can start learning how to create synthetic data that aligns with the real world domain and bridges the Sim2Real gap!

Participants will train a model on **synthetic soup can images** generated by each individual in [Falcon](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/cca0bc47-265a-4f67-843f-a434b63271b3?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3). To get the data, participants will modify different parameters in the digital twin environment and generate synthetic data that aligns with the real world test images. Participants will then test the model¡¯s performance on previously **unseen real-world images**. [Create an account to start generating data and get hands-on learning for how to optimize your synthetic data to work in the real world.](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/kaggle-page?sidebarMode=learn?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3)   

**What¡¯s New in This Challenge?**

Unlike prior editions, this challenge involves:
- Multiple instances per image.
- A heavy emphasis on dataset creation and fine-tuning.
- A chance to create your own digital twin-based data by running Scenarios on our [Falcon Cloud](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/cca0bc47-265a-4f67-843f-a434b63271b3?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3).

Users will be provided one dataset here on Kaggle that illustrates the variety of images users can generate in Falcon + users will be given access to the data creation Scenario on FalconCloud, where you can control specific Scenario parameters to create robust data that trains a high performing model. 

**Editable parameters include:**

- **Varied environment twins**
- **Camera Distance**
- **Post-Processing Grain**
- **and more!**

**What's In it for you?**  
- **Win prizes**: Cash awards, Certificates and Shoutouts on platforms like LinkedIn and Hugging Face with a chance to feature on our competition blog.  
- **Master synthetic data**: Learn skills applicable to real-world AI deployment.  
- **Boost your portfolio**: Showcase your AI & ML skills in real-world object detection.
- **[Free Falcon EDU access](http://duality.ai/edu?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3)**: Hands-on experience with high-fidelity synthetic data generation tools.  
- **Stand out to recruiters**: Rank high on Kaggle, build credibility, and showcase your skills on LinkedIn, GitHub, and resumes.
- **[Network & grow](https://discord.com/invite/dualityfalconcommunity)**: Compete with fellow students, ML engineers, and researchers, collaborating on our Discord to answer questions and build connections.

So, how well can your model **detect objects in real-world images after training only on synthetic data that you created**? Let¡¯s find out!   

---

### ?? **Objective**

- **Train on synthetic datasets**: [Use FalconCloud to iteratively generate diverse synthetic datasets that align with the real-world domain](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/kaggle-page?sidebarMode=learn?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3)
- **Test on real-world images**: Detect multiple instances of soup cans in real-world images. 
- **Score using mAP@50**: Achieve the highest **mAP@50** (Mean Average Precision at IoU 0.5) score.   


### ?? **Why Synthetic Data?**
Synthetic data is **cost-effective, scalable, and bias-free** ¨C yet synthetic-trained models often fail in real-world conditions  (referred to as the Sim2Real gap). Since 2018 [Duality] (https://www.duality.ai/?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3) has been building tools and strategies that bridge this gap, and we¡¯re sharing them with you! 

This competition demonstrates how people can use simulation to iteratively generate robust data to train AI models that work in the real world. The skills you develop in this challenge apply to: 

- Robotics 
- AI-based inspection  
- Smart Warehouses
- Augmented reality (AR) & Computer Vision applications
- And many more cutting-edge technologies!


Users must [create a free account](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/kaggle-page?sidebarMode=learn?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3) to access the cloud-based scenario used for the competition, but with the free account, users also gain the ability to download FalconEditor onto their local machines! 

FalconEditor is not a requirement for this competition, but the FalconCloud Scenario was built in FalconEditor. It is a local binary that empowers users to generate:

- Large, varied datasets using automated scripting
- Data from a wide range of environments using free environment twins from the FalconCloud library or other 3D asset sources
- Data from any sensors in Duality's sensor suite, including:
     - Infrared
     - Segmentation
     - Lidar
     - and more!

Duality also has a robust set of tutorials to teach users to generate their own data.

