---

## ?? What You're Predicting
Predict **bounding boxes** for real-world test images in YOLO format:  
- csv file of all predictions with 2 major entries being, ""image_id"", ""prediction_string""  
- Each line: `image_id"", "" object_class confidence x_center y_center width height""`  
- **Confidence scores** must be between 0 and 1

---

## ?? Acronyms
| Term | Definition |  
|------|------------|  
| **YOLO** | You Only Look Once (object detection architecture) |  
| **mAP@50** | Mean Average Precision at 50% IoU |  
| **IoU** | Intersection over Union (box overlap metric) |  

---

## ? Frequently Asked Questions

**Q: Can I use external data for training?**  
A: Yes, but only if it's created using Falcon Editor or Falcon Cloud.  

**Q: What image sizes and formats should I expect?**  
A: Synthetic images are 1980x1080px in .png format. Real test images will be 1920x1080px in .jpg format. 

**Q: How should I improve model performance and results beyond a certain point?** 
A: [Check out our tips and tricks page](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/model-and-data-improvements?sidebarMode=learn?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_3) for improving performance through scenario changes, data manipulation, model tuning, and more!",False,True
