Webinar ID: 914 0000 6479","# Dataset Description

#Introduction

This dataset explores the relationship between student habits and their academic
performance. It includes 10,000 synthetic student records with 15+ features such as
study hours, sleep patterns, social media usage, diet quality, mental health, and final
exam scores. The goal is to predict a student's final exam score based on these factors.

#Data Overview

The dataset comprises the following fields:
? student_id: Unique identifier for each student.
? age: Age of the student.
? gender: Gender of student.
? study_hours_per_day: Average number of hours spent studying per day.
? social_media_hours: Average number of hours spent on social media per day.
? netflix_hours: Average number of hours spent watching Netflix per day.
? part_time_job: Whether the student has a part-time job ('Yes' or 'No').
? attendance_percentage: Percentage of classes attended.
? sleep_hours: Average number of hours of sleep per night.
? diet_quality: Quality of diet ('Good', 'Fair', 'Poor').
? exercise_frequency: Frequency of physical exercise (scaled)
? parental_education_level: Highest education level of parents ('High School',
'Bachelor', 'Master').
? internet_quality: Quality of internet access ('Good', 'Average', 'Poor').
? mental_health_rating: Self-reported mental health rating (1 to 10 scale).
? extracurricular_participation: Participation in extracurricular activities ('Yes' or
'No').
? exam_score: Final exam score (target variable).",False,True
