9767,customer-retention-datathon-brisbane-edition,"# Overview

In this Churn Hack/Data-thon, powered by Kaggle, you'll learn and compete using the latest machine learning and data warehousing tools on Google Cloud. Rich dataset from the Media industry will allow you to derive insights that would be of most use to your business. Unleash your creativity and explore the possibilities with some examples given below: 
? 
¡¤?????????Analyzing customer churn and its reasons 
¡¤?????????Generating personalized products and loyalty offerings using predictive analytics 
¡¤?????????Insights and trend predictions 


----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [area under the ROC curve](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receiver_operating_characteristic) between the predicted probability and the observed target.


## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict a probability for the TARGET variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

msno,is_churn
    9WQJvVyggkLWsp0DLpOljfbKePSZZZeYdQvNOAkQ0bk=,0
    kTCflEFCJk6ahA8ryiGzOBQlhwEOMxuPT7gVPRzoJJ8=,1
    EgBTyrvGcPR2bjlXjPqdSkRzz1NVXVvLLdUaabKBm4I=,0
    etc.

Submission has to have 24274 rows plus a header (24275 rows in total). msno needs to match the test.csv msno.","# Dataset Description

In this challenge, you are asked to predict whether a user will churn after his/her subscription expires. Specifically, you want to forecast if a user make a new service subscription transaction within 30 days after the current membership expiration date.

The dataset contains information about music streaming service. When users signs up for the service, users can choose to either manual renew or auto-renew the service. Users can actively cancel their membership at any time.

In majority of cases, the subscription length is 30 days and a lot of users re-subscribe every month. The key fields to determine churn/renewal are transaction date, membership expiration date, and is_cancel. Note that the is_cancel field indicates whether a user actively cancels a subscription. Subscription cancellation does not imply the user has churned. A user may cancel service subscription due to change of service plans or other reasons. The criteria of ""churn"" is no new valid service subscription within 30 days after the current membership expires.

The training and the test data are selected from users whose membership expire within a certain month. The train data consists of users whose subscription expires within the month of March 2017, and the test data is with users whose subscription expires within the month of April 2017. This means we are looking at user churn or renewal roughly in the month of March 2017 for train set, and the user churn or renewal roughly in the month of April 2017. Train and test sets are split by transaction date, as well as the public and private leaderboard data.

In this dataset, you can find additional useful information, such as users behaviors or demographic information about members. 

## Files

*   **train_data.csv** - the training set
*   **members.csv** - dataset with information about members
*   **transactions.csv** - dataset with information about transactions
*   **user_logs.csv** - dataset with logs about user behaviour 
*   **kaggle_test_data.csv** - the test set


**train_data.csv** - the train set, containing the user ids and whether they have churned.
- msno: user id
- is_churn: This is the target variable. Churn is defined as whether the user did not continue the subscription within 30 days of expiration. is_churn = 1 means churn,is_churn = 0 means renewal.

**members.csv** - user information. Note that not every user in the dataset is available.
- msno
- city
- bd: age. Note: this column has outlier values ranging from -7000 to 2015, please use your judgement.
- gender
- registered_via: registration method
- registration_init_time: format %Y%m%d

**transactions.csv** - transactions data until 3/31/2017.
- msno: user id
- payment_method_id: payment method
- payment_plan_days: length of membership plan in days
- plan_list_price: in New Taiwan Dollar (NTD)
- actual_amount_paid: in New Taiwan Dollar (NTD)
- is_auto_renew
- transaction_date: format %Y%m%d
- membership_expire_date: format %Y%m%d
- is_cancel: whether or not the user canceled the membership in this transaction.

**user_logs.csv** - daily user logs describing listening behaviors of a user. Data collected until 3/31/2017.
- msno: user id
- date: format %Y%m%d
- num_25: # of songs played less than 25% of the song length
- num_50: # of songs played between 25% to 50% of the song length
- num_75: # of songs played between 50% to 75% of of the song length
- num_985: # of songs played between 75% to 98.5% of the song length
- num_100: # of songs played over 98.5% of the song length
- num_unq: # of unique songs played
- total_secs: total seconds played

 **kaggle_test_data.csv** - the test set with msno for generating predictions
- msno: user id",False,True
