<p>The model of time series is piecewise linear trend plus Brownian motion.
The length of the time series is 1000, the length of forecast is 100 points ahead.</p>
----------------------
# Evaluation

<p>The forecasting accuracy is measured by RMSE</p>","# Dataset Description

<p>The time series are located in the rows of the file. Each time series has its own Id. There is no train data, since the training for a time series can be performed by means of the time series itself.<p>
<h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>test_data.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>for_bw_onecol.csv</strong> - the sample of submission. All predictions for 100 point ahead are located in one column with Id consisting of the time series Id, '_'  and the number of the predicted point. For example, 124_17 is the Id of 17th predicted point of the 124th time series.</li></ul>",False,True
