9850,multi-class-object-detection-challenge,"# Overview

# Multi-Class Object Detection Challenge ??

## ?? Challenge Summary

Welcome to the **next evolution** of the Synthetic-to-Real Object Detection Challenge - now a **multi-class** detection task co-hosted by [**Duality AI**](https://www.duality.ai) and [**3LC**](https://3lc.ai/).

###Your Goal: 
Build an object detection model that can identify **multiple classes** (Soup + Cheerios) in **real-world test images**, using **only synthetic data** that you generate through **FalconCloud**, Duality¡¯s high-fidelity digital twin simulation platform.

**But that¡¯s not all!** This time, we¡¯re introducing a brand new collaborative workflow with **3LC**, a cutting-edge platform for identifying failure modes in AI systems. After training your model on synthetic data, you¡¯ll use **3LC¡¯s tools to analyze your model¡¯s blind spots**, then head back to FalconCloud to generate additional **targeted data** to fix them. It¡¯s an iterative, intelligent approach to training models that work *in the real world*.

[?? Watch a competition overview video on FalconCloud](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/kaggle-page#competition-description?highlight=kagg?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=overview&utm_campaign=competition_4)
[?? Watch a competition overview video on 3LC](https://youtu.be/nAotfpaOZaE)

---

### ?? What¡¯s New in This Challenge?

- **Two object classes**: Cheerios + Soup 
- **Two data generation modes**:
  - [*Randomized data scenario*](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/9e90e036-8af9-41e4-8af0-1343b8e8f467?highlight=kagg?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=overview&utm_campaign=competition_4): for rapid prototyping and large datasets
  - [*Targeted capture mode*](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/e3294c19-49d4-4f64-9ca8-8373876c2c94?highlight=kagg?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=overview&utm_campaign=competition_4): click to collect synthetic data from specific camera angles and drop locations for specialized data
- **Built-in model debugging**: Use **3LC** to find gaps in model training & data quality
- **Iterative feedback loop**: Diagnose ¡ú Generate ¡ú Retrain ¡ú Repeat

---

### ?? Learn the Real-World Workflow

In this challenge, you¡¯ll follow a simulation-to-deployment pipeline used by actual AI engineering teams:

1. **Generate synthetic training data** using FalconCloud  
2. **Train an object detection model** using 3LC (YOLOv8 recommended)  
3. **Analyze model performance** on a per-sample basis in 3LC Dashboard
4. **Identify weaknesses** in your model such as persistent false positives or false negatives
5. **Collect more data** from the Falcon scenario to address those gaps  
6. **Repeat** the process to achieve the highest mAP@50


This mimics the workflow used in fields like robotics, manufacturing QA, and autonomous systems - where collecting real-world data is expensive and iterative simulation is key.

---

### ?? Why This Challenge Matters

Synthetic data is **scalable, bias-controllable, and cost-effective**, but it still requires domain alignment to perform in the real world. **Duality** has spent years building technology to bridge that **Sim2Real gap**, and now you get hands-on access to those tools - for free.

**3LC** brings the diagnostic power: you'll learn how real ML engineers identify *why* a model fails and fix it without labeling thousands of new images.

---

### ?? What¡¯s in It for You?

-  **Win prizes**: Cash awards, certificates, and community shoutouts  
-  **Master modern workflows**: Used by robotics, CV, and inspection teams worldwide  
-  **Build your portfolio**: Perfect for resumes, GitHub, and Kaggle profiles  
-  **Get Falcon EDU  and 3LC access**: Generate and analyze high-fidelity data on your local machine  
-  **Join our community**: Network with AI engineers and students on [Duality's Discord](https://discord.com/invite/dualityfalconcommunity) and  [3LC's Discord](https://discord.com/invite/YwJcbYhA8k)

---

Ready to build an object detector that adapts, learns, and generalizes - all from simulation? Let¡¯s get started! 

----------------------
# Description

## ?? **About This Challenge** 
####**What You Need to Do**

Participants will train a model on **synthetic images** generated by each individual on FalconCloud and fine-tuned using data from 3LC. 

**Note: Something different from last competitions is that we have provided a small number real-world images for the validation. These are for validation ONLY, not training.**

Then, the trained model will then accurately predict bounding boxes for **real-world images**.  
The model¡¯s performance is evaluated based on [**mAP@50**.](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/ex2-colab-testing-output?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4#the-meaning-of-50-in-m-ap-50)   

---

## **?? How to Get Started** 
[?? Get started with FalconCloud](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/9e90e036-8af9-41e4-8af0-1343b8e8f467?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=overview&utm_campaign=competition_4)
[?? Get started with 3LC](https://account.3lc.ai/)

### Generate Initial Dataset(s)
1. [Go to the competition's page on the FalconCloud website for links to various resources, including the data-generating scenarios](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/kaggle-page?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4).
2. **[Start generating data](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/9e90e036-8af9-41e4-8af0-1343b8e8f467?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4)** using your personally selected variations. 
3. **Train a model of your choice (YOLOv8 recommended for easy itegration with Falcon and 3LC)** 
   - See the 3LC instructions for training below
4. **Run predictions on test images** 
5. **Convert the labels in .txt to a submission.csv** with our `convert_to_csv.py` file and then submit the csv file.
 `python convert_preds_to_csv.py`
6. **Confirm the format of your predictions** are correct using the submission format described in the Evaluation Section.

### Analyze Model Weakness and Improve Datasets
1. Use 3LC software to analyze model weaknesses
2. Address weakness by generating more robust and targeted data using either:
- [The automated data-generation scenario](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/9e90e036-8af9-41e4-8af0-1343b8e8f467?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4)
- [The controlled data-generation scenario](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/e3294c19-49d4-4f64-9ca8-8373876c2c94?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4)

---

## **Workflows** 

### **Generate Data on the Cloud**  
1. Create a free Falcon account and run the FalconCloud Scenario
2. Configure the parameters you think will generate the most aligned data
    - [You can reference this page](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/model-and-data-improvements?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4) for tips on effective synthetic data creation.
3. Generate multiple datasets using a variety of configurations, and use 3LC to identify dataset weaknesses
   - [Add occlusions](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/colab-ex-1-whats-next?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4)
   - [Include similar twins for improving precision](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/ex2-colab-whats-next?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4)
   - [Combine target datasets](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/documentation/ex3-colab-whats-next?sidebarMode=learn&utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4)   
   - [Use the controlled scenario to generate smaller numbers of highly specified data](https://falcon.duality.ai/secure/scenarios/edit/e3294c19-49d4-4f64-9ca8-8373876c2c94?utm_source=kaggle&utm_medium=kaggle_competition&utm_campaign=competition_4)

### **Train models and analyze training runs with 3LC**
These instructions may be run directly using [this notebook](https://github.com/3lc-ai/3lc-duality-kaggle-competition/blob/develop/Kaggle_3LC.ipynb).

See the [3LC Quickstart](https://docs.3lc.ai/3lc/latest/quickstart/quickstart.html) for more details on the sections below.

1. Create a free 3LC account
  Before getting started, make sure you have a free 3LC account. Go to https://3lc.ai and click ""Sign Up"" in the upper right corner. Sign up for a 3LC account (or log in to an existing one) using your preferred method. Then copy your API Key from the 3LC account home page.

2. Create a Python environment
  Create a Python environment called ""3LC"" using your preferred tool:
    - `python -m venv 3LC`
        - See the [Python venv documentation](https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/venv.html) for details
    - `conda create -n 3LC`
        - See the [conda documentation](https://docs.conda.io/projects/conda/en/stable/user-guide/getting-started.html) for details, or reach out if you are having trouble

3. Install the 3LC YOLO integration
  With your ""3LC"" Python environment activated, install the 3LC YOLO integration with the following command. This will also install the `3lc` Python package and all required dependencies.

  `pip install git+https://github.com/3lc-ai/3lc-ultralytics@develop`

4. Configure 3LC with your API key
  Configure 3LC to use the API key you copied earlier (or get it [here](https://account.3lc.ai/api-key)).

  `3lc login <paste API key here>`

5. Start the 3LC Object Service
  The [3LC Object Service](https://docs.3lc.ai/3lc/latest/user-guide/object-service/index.html#object-service) is responsible for serving your dataset and metrics to the 3LC Dashboard. It is started from the terminal and can be terminated by pressing Q.

  `3lc service  --no-public-examples`

6. Launch the 3LC Dashboard
  After starting the Object Service, launch the 3LC Dashboard in a browser at https://dashboard.3lc.ai and log in to your 3LC account. Your 3LC project will be displayed in the Dashboard once you begin creating 3LC data below. See the [3LC Dashboard](https://docs.3lc.ai/3lc/latest/user-guide/dashboard/index.html#dashboard-index) documentation for more details.

  Note that if you want to browse example 3LC projects (in addition to your own), you can start the Object Service in the step above without specifying the `--no-public-examples` argument.

7. Verify 3LC setup
  Now we are almost ready to start creating 3LC `Table`s for your dataset, and `Run`s for your training runs with Ultralytics YOLO.

  We first import 3LC to verify that the installation and configuration was successful. Make sure you have done the `3lc login` step above to avoid prompts or errors related to specifying a 3LC API key.

  `import tlc`

8. Creating 3LC Tables
  When you generate new images and labels in Duality, you can run the following code to create 3LC Tables for that data.

    ```python
    import tlc
    PROJECT_NAME = ""Duality-3LC-Kaggle""  # Place all 3LC Tables and Runs in the same project

    # This for loop allows you to create multiple 3LC Tables (e.g., train and val sets) in one go
    for split in [""train"", ""val""]:
        table = tlc.Table.from_yolo(
            dataset_yaml_file=""path/to/yaml/file.yaml"",  # the yolo_params.yaml file in the data folder you generate from Falcon
            split=split,
            table_name=""initial"",
            dataset_name=split,
            project_name=PROJECT_NAME,
        )
    ```
9. Joining 3LC Tables
  When you generate more data and would like to combine it with an existing 3LC Table, first create a Table with the previous snippet, then join it with your existing Table using the following code
    ```python
    import tlc
    PROJECT_NAME = ""Duality-3LC-Kaggle""  # Place all 3LC Tables and Runs in the same project

    table_1 = tlc.Table.from_url(""path/to/table_1/url"") # Hint: Copy Table URLs from Dashboard
    table_2 = tlc.Table.from_url(""path/to/table_2/url"")

    joined_table = tlc.Table.join_tables(
        tables=[table_1, table_2],
        table_name=""initial"",
        dataset_name=""joined_train"",
        project_name=PROJECT_NAME,
        description=""Join table_1 and table_2"",
    )
    ```

10. Training a YOLO model
  The following code trains a YOLO model with the 3LC YOLO integration.

    ```python
    from tlc_ultralytics import Settings, YOLO
    import tlc
    PROJECT_NAME = ""Duality-3LC-Kaggle""  # Place all 3LC Tables and Runs in the same project

    RUN_NAME = ""run-1""  # Define the run name to organize all your runs in a nice way

    # Set 3LC specific settings
    settings = Settings(
        project_name=PROJECT_NAME,
        run_name=RUN_NAME,
        run_description=""description of the run"",
    )

    # Update the URLs for the train and val tables when you make data revisions in 3LC Dashboard
    train_table = tlc.Table.from_url(""/path/to/train/table/url"")  # Hint: Copy Table URLs from Dashboard
    val_table = tlc.Table.from_url(""/path/to/val/table/url"")

    model = YOLO(""yolov8s.pt"")

    # You may add any YOLO arguments here
    model.train(
        tables={""train"": train_table, ""val"": val_table},
        settings=settings,
        epochs=5,
        agnostic_nms=True,
        project=PROJECT_NAME,
        name=RUN_NAME,
    )
    ```

  After training, the models (`best.pt` and `last.pt`) will be saved at `../Duality-3LC-Kaggle/<RUN_NAME>/weights/`.

11. Analyze training runs in the 3LC Dashboard
