# About the Tabular Playground Series

The goal of the Tabular Playground Series is to provide the Kaggle community with a variety of fairly light-weight challenges that can be used to learn and sharpen skills in different aspects of machine learning and data science. The duration of each competition will generally only last a few weeks, and may have longer or shorter durations depending on the challenge. The challenges will generally use fairly light-weight datasets that are synthetically generated from real-world data, and will provide an opportunity to quickly iterate through various model and feature engineering ideas, create visualizations, etc.

### Synthetically-Generated Datasets

Using synthetic data for Playground competitions allows us to strike a balance between having real-world data (with named features) and ensuring test labels are not publicly available. This allows us to host competitions with more interesting datasets than in the past. While there are still challenges with synthetic data generation, the state-of-the-art is much better now than when we started the Tabular Playground Series two years ago, and that goal is to produce datasets that have far fewer artifacts. Please feel free to give us feedback on the datasets for the different competitions so that we can continue to improve!",,False,True
9855,msa-challenge-at-the-4th-pazhou-ai-competition,"# Overview

### Important Notice
To officially participate in the competition, you must joint and submit results on the Kaggle competition page, and complete the official registration forms:
- For participants **from outside China Mainland**, please complete [Google Forms](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScjCk7rJXqsst8HotT4-jiWJ9X-Emd7PlIuH1U8fgnoyJAsXQ/viewform),
[https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScjCk7rJXqsst8HotT4-jiWJ9X-Emd7PlIuH1U8fgnoyJAsXQ/viewform](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScjCk7rJXqsst8HotT4-jiWJ9X-Emd7PlIuH1U8fgnoyJAsXQ/viewform)
- For participates **from China Mainland**, please register via [Pazhou Algorithm Competition Registration Form](https://www.aicompetition-pz.com/topic_register?type=2).
[https://www.aicompetition-pz.com/topic_register?type=2](https://www.aicompetition-pz.com/topic_register?type=2)

### Overall Introduction
This competition is a part of **International AI Competition of the 4th Pazhou AI Competition** orgnized by Guangzhou Municipal People's Government and Chinese Association for Artificial Intelligence (CAAI). Detail information about this grand competition can be found on [https://www.aicompetition-pz.com/topic](https://www.aicompetition-pz.com/topic).

The specific topic here is **¡°Cross-lingual Multimodal Explainable Sentiment Recognition¡±**. Participants are required to design and implement a multimodal sentiment analysis model capable of processing multilingual (English and Chinese) multimodal data, accurately recognizing sentiment polarity, and possessing the following capabilities:
1. **Cross-lingual analytical capability**: The model should handle both English and Chinese data with good transfer and generalization performance across languages.
2. **Model explainability**: The model should clearly demonstrate the contribution of each modality and its specific features in sentiment recognition, thereby improving transparency and trustworthiness.

### Total Prizes Available: £¤190,000
- **First Prize: £¤100,000**
- **Second Prize: £¤50,000**
- **Third Prize: £¤20,000**
- **Fourth and Fifth Prize: £¤10,000**
