----------------------
# Evaluation

The ultimate goal of this competition is to develop algorithms that can accurately identify as many true pottery sherd connections as possible. Success in this endeavor will directly facilitate the virtual reconstruction of original vessel forms, providing crucial insights for archaeological analysis. Submissions will be evaluated based on a combination of metrics designed to assess different aspects of this complex task: 

**Matching Accuracy (70%) **
	This metric will evaluate the correctness of predicted pairwise connections between pottery sherds. Participants will submit pairs of sherd_ids that they believe are connected. The judging panel will verify the results through objective algorithms and manual cross-referencing, ensuring the accuracy and fairness of the evaluation.

**Object Completeness (15%) **
	This metric measures the overall proportion of the pottery vessel that can be restored after assembly (based on comparison with reference shapes). This metric aims to reward solutions that not only find correct individual pairings but also contribute to forming larger, more continuous fragments of the original vessels. This will be evaluated by quantitatively comparing predicted vessel reconstruction data (such as 3D models or key geometric points) with provided reference shapes.

**Solution Report Quality & Innovation (15%) **
	Model Robustness and Speed: The number of pottery sherds that can be processed, runtime, and other relevant factors will be considered to assess the model's effectiveness in practical applications.
	Innovation and Technical Documentation Quality: The innovativeness of the model concept, code standardization, completeness of documentation, etc., will be evaluated.	


