# Q&A

Q: **What format should I use to submit my results?**   
A: Please pack your submission results into a zip file. The zip file should contain a CSV file, assembled images for all groups (each group must include both the exterior and interior images of the pottery shards), main code files (Python or other supported platform languages), 3D model files (if any, optional), and a technical documentation (PDF).
Please send the documents to h690@uic.edu.cn as well.

*Regarding the CSV file:*   
Please refer to the `submission_template.csv` file in the root directory.   
Your CSV should contain only two columns: Assembly Group name(`Assembly Group`), and all image filenames included in that group (`image_id`both exterior and interior sides must be listed).   

*Naming conventions*:   
Name assembly groups in the format AssemblyGroup* (e.g., AssemblyGroup1).   
Name the exterior and interior images for each group as:   
`AssemblyGroup*_exterior.jpg`   
`AssemblyGroup*_interior.jpg`   
Use the original image filenames from `h690/h690/shred_images` in the `image_id` column of your CSV.   

You may organize your files as follows:   
```
Submission.zip
©À©¤©¤ submission.csv
©À©¤©¤ AssemblyGroup1_exterior.jpg
©À©¤©¤ AssemblyGroup1_interior.jpg
©À©¤©¤ AssemblyGroup2_exterior.jpg
©À©¤©¤ AssemblyGroup2_interior.jpg
©À©¤©¤ 3DModel/          [Folder]
©À©¤©¤ SourceCode/       [Folder]
©¸©¤©¤ Doc.pdf
```

