9904,srifoton-25-machine-learning-competition,"# Overview

Selamat datang di kompetisi Machine Learning Srifoton 2025! 

Berikut merupakan Kaggle Competition sebagai wadah penyeleksian peserta Machine Learning Srifoton 2025, akan diadakan 2 babak berupa babak seleksi dan babak final. Penilaian kompetisi akan menggunakan fitur evaluasi Macro F1-score dari Kaggle. 
----------------------
# Description

Kompetisi ini bertujuan mengembangkan model Machine Learning yang akurat dalam memprediksi dan mendeteksi penyakit pernapasan melalui citra X-Ray paru-paru pasien. Para peserta dalam melakukan pembuatan model, peserta diperkenankan untuk menggunakan berbagai metode, tools, library, atau framework apa saja.


----------------------
# Evaluation

Dalam kompetisi ini, kami akan menggunakan Macro F1-Score sebagai metrik evaluasi utama untuk mengukur kinerja model pendeteksi penyakit paru-paru. Macro F1-Score memberikan bobot yang sama untuk setiap kelas, terlepas dari jumlah sampelnya. Sehingga memudahkan untuk mengevaluasi model pada dataset yang tidak seimbang, karena model tidak akan bias hanya pada kelas yang memiliki jumlah data terbanyak.

Untuk menghitung Macro F1-Score, diperlukan menghitung Precision dan Recall untuk setiap kelas secara individual terlebih dahulu.

Menghitung Precision :

$$Precision = \frac{TP}{TP + FP}$$
- TP (True Positive) : Jumlah data yang diprediksi benar sebagai kelas target.
- FP (False Positive): Jumlah data yang salah diprediksi sebagai kelas target.

Menghitung Recall :

$$Recall = \frac{TP}{TP + FN}$$
- FN (False Negative) : Jumlah data yang salah diprediksi sebagai kelas target (model tidak mendeteksinya).

Setelah mendapatkan Precision dan Recall setiap kelas, maka dapat dihitung F1-Score masing-masing kelas dengan : $$F1 Score = 2 \cdot \frac{Precision \cdot Recall}{Precision + Recall}$$

Macro F1-Score kemudian dihitung sebagai rata-rata dari semua F1-Score per kelas.
$$Macro\ F1-Score = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} F1-Score_i$$

---

##Submission File
Untuk setiap ID pada test file, Anda harus memprediksi id gambar dan label penyakitnya. File submisi harus memiliki header dan mengikuti format berikut :

```
Id,Predicted
test_0000.jpeg,0
test_0001.jpeg,0
seterusnya hingga Bacteria habis
test_0100.jpeg,1 
... (hingga Corona habis)
test_0200.jpeg,2 
... (hingga Normal habis)
test_0300.jpeg,3 
... (hingga Tuberculosis habis)
test_0400.jpeg,4 
... (hingga Viral Pneumonia habis)
```","# Dataset Description

## Folders

*   **train** - berisi dataset gambar untuk training
*   **test** - berisi dataset gambar untuk test
*   **val** - berisi dataset gambar untuk validasi",False,True
9905,sai-challenge,"# Overview

**?????? Welcome to the ScienceON AI (SAI) Challenge ¡ª Hosted by KISTI!**

The **ScienceON AI (SAI) Challenge** invites you to tackle one of the most exciting frontiers in AI: retrieving and summarizing scientific knowledge using large language models (LLMs). **Organized by KISTI (Korea Institute of Science and Technology Information), this challenge is part of our ongoing mission to build powerful AI tools for accelerating scientific discovery.** Your task will involve processing complex queries, retrieving relevant information from a scientific knowledge base, and generating accurate, fluent, and well-cited answers. **Whether you're a researcher, student, or developer, this is your opportunity to contribute to the future of AI-assisted science!??**
----------------------
# Prizes & Awards

**?? Awards (Top 3 Teams): KISTI President¡¯s Award (certificate) & Bluetooth speaker**
**?? (RDGENAI 2025 Workshop Participants)One phone charger per attending challenge participant ¡ª first-come, first-served (50 units)**
----------------------
# Description

In this challenge, you¡¯ll work with SAI (ScienceON AI), an intelligent scientific article retrieval and summarization system developed by **KISTI¡¯s ScienceON platform**. SAI is built upon a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework that integrates information retrieval.

?? **What We Provide**
You will be given:
      1)  **A RAG-based baseline system** (SAI) to kickstart your development,
      2) **A dataset of 50 real-world scientific questions**, each **accompanied by automatically retrieved articles** and expert-annotated ground truth answers for evaluation.

?? **Your Task**
Your goal is to **enhance the performance and reliability of the baseline RAG pipeline by implementing an API-based system by integrating with your own methods** that can:
   1)**Retrieve relevant documents** using or **extending the provided SAI retrieval methods**
   2) Apply your own methods to **re-rank documents** to select the most contextually relevant information
   3) Apply your own methods to **expand selected articles** to enrich the input for generation
   4)**Refer the reference documents clearly and accurately** within your generated answers
   5)**Generate fluent, factually correct, and concise summaries** that answer the original questions

By integrating your own reranking strategies, enriching the retrieved content through passage expansion, exploring complementary tools like MCP and other various methods, your challenge is to enhance the SAI RAG baseline system and generate higher-quality answers for the 50 provided scientific questions!??

?**Note:** **People who will be in** **top-6 ranking until September 10, 2025**, **they need to submit their environment setting and all pipeline codes to us! The final pipelines, results and code will be evaluated by our team!**
----------------------
# Final Results of Competition

**1st ranking: ???**
**2nd ranking: DILAB**
**3rd ranking: Paul Kamau**
----------------------
# How Kaggle Competition Work 

**1.Enter the Challenge**
Review the competition overview, agree to the official rules, and get access to the full dataset.

**2.Start Building**
Use the provided test data, either locally or on Kaggle Notebooks (a free, no-setup Jupyter environment with GPU support).

**3. Submit Your Results**
Generate your predictions and upload them to Kaggle to receive your evaluation score.

**Track Your Progress**
Check the leaderboard to see how your solution compares to others in real-time.


**! Note: Please check the competition page regularly!**

----------------------
# What Data Will I Use in This Competition

??In this competition, in order to test your pipeline which is integrated to our SAI RAG baseline, you need to use `'test.csv' `file which is located in ['Data'](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/sai-challenge/data) tab as well. 

??In the `'test.csv'` file, there are questions and their retrieved articles via our SAI baseline. 
----------------------
# SAI RAG Baseline

