`python scienceon_api_example.py`

4. When you executed this command, for a specific query, you will get the answer and retrieved documents by our baseline.


??**Required Computational Source to Execute the SAI RAG Baseline**
1. Once you improved our SAI baseline, we restrict the computational source with 50 GB. When we obtain your code, we need to be able to execute your pipeline with the GPU which has max 50 GB and less memory.
----------------------
# How to Submit Your Prediction

????Once you¡¯re ready to make a submission and get on the leaderboard:
1. Click on the **Submit Predictions** button.
2. **Upload a CSV file in the submission file format.**  You¡¯re able to submit 20 submissions a day.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F28059272%2Fe7c386b850610802290a0303d047e168%2Fresult_submission_page.png?generation=1753835502875352&alt=media)

??**Submission File Format**
Your submission file must contain:
1.The **generated answers** as a result of your pipeline execution,
2.The **retrieved articles per each question** as a result of your pipeline execution.

**Those are the final columns that your submission file must have:**
['id', 'Question', 'SAI_Answer', 'translated_question', 'translated_SAI_answer', 'retrieved_article_name_1', ...., 'retrieved_article_name_50', 'prediction_retrieved_article_name_1', ..., 'prediction_retrieved_article_name_50', 'Prediction', 'elapsed_times']. 
**Please make sure that your 'submission.csv' file contains the following columns!**

?**Note: Since you have several testing right in the kaggle leaderboard in a day, please make sure your pipeline and then submit your final ready-to-submit work to us.**
----------------------
# Evaluation

In this challenge, your system will be evaluated on both the quality of the generated answers and the efficiency of your retrieval and summarization process. We use a custom composite metric that reflects real-world expectations of accurate, relevant, and timely scientific information delivery.

**?? Individual Metrics**
Your submission will be scored using the following four metrics:

**BLEU Score**: Measures the n-gram overlap between your generated answer and the human-annotated ground truth. This reflects surface-level fluency and phrasing accuracy.

**METEOR Score**: Goes beyond surface overlap by considering synonyms, stemming, and word order, making it better at evaluating semantic similarity between the generated and ground truth answers.

**Retrieval Accuracy**: Evaluates how many of the documents you used (via citation or retrieval) are part of the human-annotated reference set. This score rewards systems that retrieve and rely on the correct scientific sources.

**Execution Time**: Measures the total time your system takes to process all 1 question, including retrieval, reranking, and generation. Faster systems score better on this metric encouraging efficient implementations.

**?? Final Composite Score**
The final score is a weighted combination of the above components:
Overall quality score is calculated as mean of BLEU, METEOR and Retrieval Accuracy score.
Final score is **average  of overall quality score and execution time.** Once we calculate the this average of quality score and execution time, we take the average of 50 final score which is the leaderboard ranking score.
----------------------
# Frequently Asked Questions (FQA)

?**I could not get my ScienceON API Key yet. What is the reason?**
????In order to get ScienceON API key to execute our SAI RAG baseline, you need to wait 1-2 days that our team will confirm your access after you finishes your application. Therefore, we recommend to apply for API key when you start to this competition.


?**I got my ScienceON API key, however still I cannot run the SAI RAG baseline code. What is the reason?**
????We recommend you to check whether you assigned your MAC address with your IP address. There is another important information that **you can request ScienceON API key from us maximum 10 times.**


?**How do I contact to get support?**
????You can ask your questions via **[Discussion](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/sai-challenge/discussion?sort=hotness)** section. We will follow your questions frequently in there.


?**How to create my own team?**
????Once you join the competition, a team is assigned to you in the **[Team](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/sai-challenge/team)** section, so you can invite your other team members in there as well. Please check the relevant section.
----------------------
# Host Information

This competition is hosted by **Korean Institute of Science and Technology (KISTI)**, which is research institute located in Daejeon, South Korea.",,False,True
