9920,evaluate-othello-boards,"# Overview

Othello, a variant of [Reversi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reversi), is an abstract strategy game in which two players compete for territory by placing and flipping two-sided discs.

Given a variety of board positions to analyse, can you train an effective model for predicting turn-player evaluation scores?
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on [Root Mean Squared Error](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root_mean_square_deviation), which measures the average magnitude of prediction errors.

## Submission File
For each ```""id""``` in the test set, you must predict a value for the ```""turn_player_advantage""``` variable. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    id,turn_player_advantage
    6401,0.0
    6402,0.0
    6403,0.0
    etc.",,False,True
