9991,eo-summer-school-2025-hackathon-ndvi-reconstruct,"# Overview

Satellite imagery is often affected by clouds and other artifacts, which can obscure or distort the data. Although such contaminants are filtered out, many applications, particularly machine learning models, require complete datasets to be effective. The task of reconstructing missing values, commonly referred to in the literature as gap-filling or time-series reconstruction, is the focus of this challenge.
You will work with real NDVI data derived from satellite imagery at a 30 m resolution. The dataset covers three tiles (each approximately 120 km ¡Á 120 km): one central tile, along with one adjacent tile to the east and one to the west. For each tile, cloud-free observations are available over a 10-year period, with a temporal resolution of 16 days. In addition, 10,000 time series have been sampled from pixels within the central tile. To these time series, we have artificially introduced an additional 25% of missing values.
Your goal is to reconstruct the missing values as accurately as possible, using both the remaining values within each time series and information from the neighboring tiles. The quality of your solution will be evaluated based on the Root Mean Square Error (RMSE)¡ªthe lower, the better.
----------------------
# Description

You will work with real NDVI data derived from satellite imagery at a 30 m resolution. The dataset covers three tiles (each approximately 120 km ¡Á 120 km): one central tile, along with one adjacent tile to the east and one to the west. For each tile, cloud-free observations are available over a 10-year period, with a temporal resolution of 16 days. In addition, 10,000 time series have been sampled from pixels within the central tile. To these time series, we have artificially introduced an additional 25% of missing values.

$$\textrm{NDVI}=\frac{\mathrm{NIR} - \mathrm{Red}}{\mathrm{NIR} + \mathrm{Red}}\ $$

----------------------
# Evaluation

Your goal is to reconstruct the missing values as accurately as possible, using both the remaining values within each time series and information from the neighboring tiles. The quality of your solution will be evaluated based on the Root Mean Square Error (RMSE)¡ªthe lower, the better.

**Check *Discussion* for more information on how to create a proper submission!**
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F28558337%2F60e6db84de7f5dac10b864e860dd53a3%2FScreenshot%20from%202025-09-01%2013-50-45.png?generation=1756727469213458&alt=media)

## Submission File
A .csv with the reconstructed values in the indices specified by the testing.csv file.","# Dataset Description

## Files

*   **train.csv** - The time series that need to be reconstructed, the rows are samples IDs, while columns the corresponding timeframe. Each element of the .csv can eather have and NDVI values or a not a value, in case the data is a gap.
*   **test.csv** - This specifies where the reconstruction will be evaluated (based on sample ID and timefreame) 
*   **sample_submission.csv** - a sample submission file in the correct format, corresponding to the NDVI values in the combinations of indices specified by test.csv.

## Additional data from neighbor tiles

Additional data from complete time-series (excluding gaps already present) from neighbor tiles will be released on Zenodo at https://zenodo.org/records/17017626.

As you will notice each image associated to a timframe contain several gaps. This is be due to missing Landsat scenes, cloud presence, and other sources of contaminants.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F28558337%2F234579aa3adda64fef939699a1b545f2%2FScreenshot%20from%202025-09-01%2013-52-42.png?generation=1756727714377673&alt=media)

## *In discussion you will find more info and some code on how to access the data!*",False,True
9992,seminar-soal-ioai,"# Overview

##**BACA DESKRIPSI SOAL DENGAN BAIK-BAIK.**



----------------------
# Description

Nesy adalah seorang pelukis handal yang dikenal akan karya-karya lukisnya yang unik dan konsisten. Ia selalu melukis di atas kanvas berukuran 9 kali 9. Meskipun terbatas dalam jumlah cat yang dimiliki, Nesy mampu menciptakan karya luar biasa. Karena keterbatasan tersebut, beberapa bagian lukisan dibiarkan berwarna putih (belum dicat), sementara sisanya diberi warna menggunakan skala abu-abu.

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F27319419%2F17e1385130f9b8d1cf7502c4d785c8ba%2Fgrayscale_gradient.png?generation=1750221778247110&alt=media)

Beberapa tahun kemudian, lukisan-lukisan Nesy dipajang di sebuah museum seni. Namun, saat Nesy datang mengunjungi pameran tersebut, ia menyadari sesuatu yang janggal: beberapa lukisan tampak seperti dipalsukan! Meskipun ukurannya sama dan warna-warna yang digunakan mirip, ada pola tertentu yang membuatnya curiga.

Sebagai sahabat setia Nesy dan juga seorang ahli teknologi, kamu memutuskan untuk membantu. Tugasmu adalah membuat model deteksi untuk membedakan antara lukisan asli karya Nesy atau lukisan palsu yang mungkin dibuat oleh pemalsu.

Berikut sebagai contoh pada lukisan tersebut.
![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F27319419%2Fede813468d13d8da462c7a94800c2d2b%2Fboard_0_label_1_scale_14_frame_red.png?generation=1750221334725424&alt=media)
----------------------
# Evaluation

Terdapat 3 subtask yang harus kamu selesaikan berdasarkan dataset lukisan:

