*   Generate your API [Keys](https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys) after logging in
*   Start building: JavaScript and Python snippets can be found [here](https://docs.fal.ai/model-apis/quickstart)

----------------------
# Submission Instructions

A submission is comprised of the following:

1. Kaggle Writeup  
   1. Attached Video Demo
   2. Attached Public Project Link

### 1. Kaggle Writeup

Your submission must be a Kaggle Writeup and it must be attached to this competition page. 

Ensure you address the following sections in your writeup. 

* **Project Title:** A creative and descriptive name for the project.  
* **Problem Statement:** A brief write-up (max 200 words) detailing which Gemini 2.5 Flash Image features were used and how they are central to the application.


To create a new Writeup, click on the ""New Writeup"" button [here](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/banana/projects). After you have saved your Writeup, you should see a ""Submit"" button in the top right corner. 

Each team is limited to submitting only a single Writeup, but that same Writeup can be un-submitted, edited, and re-submitted as many times as you'd like. Your Writeup should contain a summary of your overall project along with links to supporting resources. 

**Your final Submission must be made prior to the deadline. Any un-submitted or draft Writeups by the competition deadline will not be considered by the Judges.**

Note: If you attach a private Kaggle Resource to your public Kaggle Writeup, your private Resource will automatically be made public after the deadline.

#### a\.?Attached Video Demo

An engaging video demonstrating your project in action. It must be posted publicly (YouTube, X/Twitter, etc.) and a direct link provided. It must be viewable by the judges without requiring a login and should be attached to your Writeup.

#### b\.?Attached Public Project Link

A URL to your working product or interactive demo. Consider using AI Studio apps, which are the fastest way to build prototypes using the Gemini API. This allows judges to experience your project firsthand, if applicable. It should be publicly accessible and not require a login or paywall. If a live demo is not feasible, a link to your public code repository (e.g., GitHub) is required, including detailed setup instructions.",,True,True
9999,2025-uml-501-lab-3q14-kaggle-hack-i,"# Overview


## Rules:
