# ?? The Final Trial: Recognition  

You have mastered the cold logic of **legendary power** and the high-stakes strategy of the **duel**.  
You¡¯ve protected your team and earned your place as a formidable trainer. ??  

But now, for your **final trial**, the battlefield fades¡­  
and the challenge shifts to the **screen**.  

This is a test recognized by masters and novices alike ¡ª  
a ritual, a game, and the ultimate measure of a true **Pok¨¦mon expert**.  

Will your eyes and instincts guide you true?  
Or will the final challenge expose your limits? ?

----------------------
# Description

# ??? The Final Trial: Who¡¯s That Pok¨¦mon?  

(? Dramatic, up-beat music begins...)  
The screen flashes. A shadowy figure, silhouetted against a brilliant blue background, strikes a pose.  
You can almost hear the iconic announcer¡¯s voice echo in your mind.  

You see the outline ¡ª the shape, maybe a hint of a tail or a wing.  
It could be anyone! You have only a few moments before the brilliant reveal.  
Your heart pounds. You shout a name at the screen!  

This is the feeling, the pure joy and suspense, that you must capture in code.  

---

### ? Your Mission  
This is more than a game ¡ª it¡¯s the **culmination of your journey**.  
You are tasked with creating this world¡¯s first-ever **visual Pok¨¦dex**.  

Forget statistics; this is about **instinct and sight**.  
Using a vast library of images, you will train a **deep learning model**  
to look at any Pok¨¦mon and declare its name with unwavering confidence.  

Engineer an algorithm that feels the suspense, analyzes the silhouette,  
and triumphantly shouts:  
**¡°It¡¯s Pikachu!¡±** ? before the lights come back on.  

Your legacy awaits. ??

----------------------
# Evaluation

A master's eye does not waver.  
The evaluation for this final, ultimate challenge will be **Categorical Accuracy**.  

Your model will be presented with a series of **unseen Pok¨¦mon images**, and for each one, it must provide a **single, definitive answer**.  
The final score will be the **percentage of Pok¨¦mon correctly identified** ¡ª a direct measure of your model's real-world performance.  

Can your algorithm achieve the instant, certain recognition of a **true Pok¨¦mon Master**?  
We are about to find out.  

---

## Submission File  

For each **id** (the file name without png) in the test set, you must predict the name of the pokemon in the **label** variable.",,False,True
10016,desafio-de-similaridade-empresarial,"# Overview

Voc¨º receber¨¢ informa??es anonimizadas sobre empresas brasileiras, contendo dados sobre sua estrutura, localiza??o e indicadores econ?micos.

Seu desafio ¨¦ encontrar e retornar os **K (onde K = 5)** vizinhos mais similares do conjunto de treinamento para cada empresa do conjunto de teste, com base nas vari¨¢veis fornecidas.

----------------------
# Description

O objetivo ¨¦, para cada empresa em `test.csv`, identificar os **5 registros** de `train.csv` que sejam considerados mais similares com base em suas caracter¨ªsticas. Essa ¨¦ uma **competi??o n?o supervisionada**, ou seja, n?o h¨¢ uma vari¨¢vel-alvo ¨²nica ou uma ""empresa correta"". A avalia??o ser¨¢ feita comparando sua submiss?o com o arquivo de solu??o fornecido (`solution.csv`), que foi gerado usando uma m¨¦trica de refer¨ºncia interna.

**Arquivos fornecidos**

- `train.csv`: o conjunto base de empresas com atributos anonimizados.  
- `test.csv`: as empresas-alvo para as quais voc¨º deve encontrar os 5 registros mais similares.  
- `sample_submission.csv`: um exemplo de arquivo de submiss?o v¨¢lido no formato esperado.

----------------------
# Evaluation

As submiss?es ser?o avaliadas usando a m¨¦trica **Precision@K**, que mede a propor??o de IDs submetidos que coincidem com os IDs da solu??o oficial para cada item de teste.

$$
P@K = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N \frac{|\text{submission}_i \cap \text{solution}_i|}{K}
$$

**Arquivo de Submiss?o**

Para cada `id_test`, voc¨º deve submeter uma string contendo os IDs do conjunto de treinamento separados por espa?o, conforme o exemplo em `sample_submission.csv`.

```csv
id_test,neighbors
20,""45 12 78 9 33""
42,""7 2 85 19 40""
```

Os `id_test` que voc¨º dever¨¢ utilizar s?o ""42"", ""20"", ""1000"", ""4500"", ""10000"", ""189"", ""251"", ""25192"", ""122961"", ""112670"", ""2"". A sequ¨ºncia deles n?o precisa seguir essa ordem.",,False,True
