10025,modelify-round-1,"# Overview

# ?? The Duelist¡¯s Prophecy: Prologue  

You awaken, not in your own world, but in a realm echoing with the spirit of a **post-modern samurai**. ??  
This alternate Pok¨¦mon world is untamed, beautiful, and dangerous. Here, survival and honor are earned through strength, strategy, and the bond you share with your Pok¨¦mon companions.  

---

## ?? Your First Quest: Perception  

The Pok¨¦dex hasn¡¯t been invented, and while whispers of all-powerful **""Legendary"" Pok¨¦mon** ride the wind, no one knows how to find them.  
They are the keys to ultimate power, but they walk among common Pok¨¦mon, their true nature hidden.  

To build a team worthy of a champion, you must first **learn to see the unseen**.  
You cannot rely on myth or rumor; you must rely on **data**.  

---

## ?? The Scroll of Knowledge  

You have managed to collect a scroll containing the base statistics of hundreds of Pok¨¦mon ¡ª  
their speed, their attack, their raw power.  

Hidden within these numbers is a **pattern**, a signature that screams *¡°Legendary.¡±*  

---

## ?? Your Mission  

Forge an algorithm capable of piercing this veil of secrecy.  

This is more than just a challenge; it is your **first step to becoming a legend** yourself.  
Train your model, trust your instincts, and separate the gods from the creatures.  

---

## ?? The Path of the Master  

Identify the Legendary Pok¨¦mon before they fall into the wrong hands,  
and carve your name into the history of this world.  

? The path of the master begins now. Are you ready? ?

----------------------
# Description

# ?? The Duelist¡¯s Prophecy  

Step into an alternate Pok¨¦mon world, a realm echoing with the spirit of a **post-modern samurai**.  
In this untamed and dangerous land, survival and honor are earned through strategy, strength,  
and the bond with your Pok¨¦mon.  

**Legendary Pok¨¦mon** ¡ª beings of immense power ¡ª walk hidden among the ordinary.  

Your task is to **detect the unseen using data**. You have collected a scroll containing base statistics ¡ª  
speed, attack, defense, and more ¡ª of hundreds of Pok¨¦mon.  
Within these numbers lies a signature that reveals which Pok¨¦mon are Legendary.  

Your mission: **build an algorithm capable of identifying them.**  

This competition is more than just predictive modeling; it is a test of **observation, insight, and skill**.  
Train your model, trust your instincts, and separate the gods from the creatures.  

Identify the Legendary Pok¨¦mon before they fall into the wrong hands,  
and carve your name into the history of this world. ?

----------------------
# Evaluation

This is a test of precision. Submissions will be judged by **Accuracy**¡ªthe share of predictions your model gets right. A perfect classifier scores **1.00**, while random guessing hovers near chance for a balanced set. Accuracy measures how often you correctly name each Pok¨¦mon as **mundane** or **Legendary**. Your model must choose decisively at prediction time; we¡¯ll compare its chosen labels to the truth and count the victories. The more battles won, the higher your Accuracy¡ªsimple, sharp, and unforgiving.","# Dataset Description

# ?? Pok¨¦mon Legendary Classification Dataset  

## ?? Objective  
Predict whether a Pok¨¦mon is **Legendary (1)** or **Not Legendary (0)**.  

---

## ?? Dataset Info  
- **Total samples:** 640  
- **Target:** `Legendary` (0 / 1)  
- **Features:** `Name`, `HP`, `Attack`, `Defense`, `Sp. Atk`, `Sp. Def`, `Speed`, `Generation`, `Legendary`  
- **Class distribution:** ~8¨C10% Legendary Pok¨¦mon *(imbalanced dataset)*  

---

## ?? Files  
- **pokemon.csv** ¡ú Training data with features and labels  
- **test.csv** ¡ú Test features only  
- **sample_submission.csv** ¡ú Submission format (`id`, `Legendary`)",False,True
10026,modelify-round-2,"# Overview

# ?? Congratulations, Seeker  

Congratulations, Seeker. Your senses are sharp, and you have successfully **identified the legends** hiding in plain sight. ??  
Now, with your potential team assembled, you face a terrifying truth about this world: **there are no Pok¨¦mon Centers.**  
Every battle is a duel to the end, and when a Pok¨¦mon is defeated, it is **gone... forever.** ??  

The bond you forge with your Pok¨¦mon is a fragile one, and **victory is the only thing that can protect it.**  

---

You cannot afford to be reckless. Before you send your trusted companion into the arena, you must be **certain of the outcome.**  
Your next challenge is to become a **grandmaster of strategy, a seer of combat.**  

Using a dataset chronicling **thousands of past duels**, you must build a model that can **predict the winner** of any given fight.  
?? Analyze the combatants, weigh their strengths and weaknesses, and **calculate the odds.**  

---

This tool will be your **guide, your crystal ball ??**, helping you navigate the **high-stakes world of Pok¨¦mon battles**  
where the price of failure is **absolute. ??**

----------------------
# Evaluation

In the heat of battle, there is no room for ambiguity¡ªthere is only a winner and a loser. Therefore, submissions for this round will be judged on **Categorical Accuracy**. This metric is straightforward and unforgiving: it measures the percentage of battles where your model correctly predicted the victor. Every correct prediction is a Pok¨¦mon saved; every failure is a potential loss. Strive for the highest accuracy, as your team's very survival depends on the precision of your predictions.","# Dataset Description

# ?? The Duelist's Prophecy  

Welcome, Duelist. Your journey has led you to the heart of this world's conflict: the **honor-bound arena** where legends are forged and tragically broken.  

Now that you have a team, you must guide them through the perilous path of combat, where every victory brings glory and every defeat is an **irreversible farewell**.  
Your **predictive skills** are the only thing standing between your Pok¨¦mon and eternal silence.  

---

## ?? The Challenge  

Will you be able to **predict the outcome** of future matches?  
Can you become a **seer of combat**, gazing into the future to protect those you lead?  

---

## ?? Ancient Sources of Knowledge  

- **The Codex of Beings (`pokemons.csv`)**  
  A sacred scroll containing the very essence of every known Pok¨¦mon. ??  
  Within, you will find their characteristics, their strengths, and their weaknesses.  
  The first column marks the creature's unique identifier, a key to its identity.  

- **The Chronicle of Duels (`battles.csv`)**  
  A grim but invaluable record of historical combats.  
  This chronicle details thousands of past battles, listing the two combatants and, most importantly, the victor.  
  Study these ghosts of the past, for their sacrifices hold the key to your future.  

---

## ?? A Sacred Rule  

A critical piece of lore must be understood:  

The Pok¨¦mon listed **first** in the chronicle is the one who **strikes first**.  
This singular advantage ¡ª the **honor of the first strike** ¡ª can change the tide of battle in a heartbeat.  

A swift aggressor might fell a more powerful foe before they can even mount a defense.  
You must weigh this tactical truth in all your predictions.  

---

## ?? Your Goal  

Forge a **Machine Learning model** ¡ª a crystal ball of code ¡ª  
able to consult these ancient texts and **prophesy the result of future Pok¨¦mon combats**.  

You will be presented with **The Gauntlet of Fate (`test.csv`)**,  
a scroll of challenges yet to come.",False,True
10027,modelify-round-3,"# Overview

# ?? The Final Trial: Recognition  

You have mastered the cold logic of **legendary power** and the high-stakes strategy of the **duel**.  
You¡¯ve protected your team and earned your place as a formidable trainer. ??  

But now, for your **final trial**, the battlefield fades¡­  
and the challenge shifts to the **screen**.  

This is a test recognized by masters and novices alike ¡ª  
a ritual, a game, and the ultimate measure of a true **Pok¨¦mon expert**.  

Will your eyes and instincts guide you true?  
Or will the final challenge expose your limits? ?

----------------------
# Description

# ??? The Final Trial: Who¡¯s That Pok¨¦mon?  

(? Dramatic, up-beat music begins...)  
The screen flashes. A shadowy figure, silhouetted against a brilliant blue background, strikes a pose.  
You can almost hear the iconic announcer¡¯s voice echo in your mind.  

You see the outline ¡ª the shape, maybe a hint of a tail or a wing.  
It could be anyone! You have only a few moments before the brilliant reveal.  
Your heart pounds. You shout a name at the screen!  

This is the feeling, the pure joy and suspense, that you must capture in code.  

---

### ? Your Mission  
This is more than a game ¡ª it¡¯s the **culmination of your journey**.  
You are tasked with creating this world¡¯s first-ever **visual Pok¨¦dex**.  

Forget statistics; this is about **instinct and sight**.  
Using a vast library of images, you will train a **deep learning model**  
to look at any Pok¨¦mon and declare its name with unwavering confidence.  

Engineer an algorithm that feels the suspense, analyzes the silhouette,  
and triumphantly shouts:  
**¡°It¡¯s Pikachu!¡±** ? before the lights come back on.  

Your legacy awaits. ??

----------------------
# Evaluation

A master's eye does not waver.  
The evaluation for this final, ultimate challenge will be **Categorical Accuracy**.  

Your model will be presented with a series of **unseen Pok¨¦mon images**, and for each one, it must provide a **single, definitive answer**.  
The final score will be the **percentage of Pok¨¦mon correctly identified** ¡ª a direct measure of your model's real-world performance.  

Can your algorithm achieve the instant, certain recognition of a **true Pok¨¦mon Master**?  
We are about to find out.  

---

## Submission File  

For each **id** (the file name without png) in the test set, you must predict the name of the pokemon in the **label** variable.",,False,True
