10058,hw-1-instruction-classifier,"# Overview

# **Competition Title: Instruction Classifier**

## Objective
The goal of this competition is to develop a model capable of classifying instructions in sentences. Given input sentences that may contain instructional content, participants are tasked with labeling each sentence as one of three categories: modify (0), insert (1), or delete (2).

## Context
The competition focuses on instruction sentences generated by GPT models. These instructions represent common operations in text editing and document manipulation contexts.

## Dataset
The dataset for this competition is derived from GPT-generated content, which consists of:
- **Sentence**: The text serving as the input to be classified
- **Label**: The ground truth classification (modify = 0, insert = 1, delete = 2)
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions will be evaluated using precision, recall, and F1-score, ensuring robust performance on both detecting and avoiding false positives.
- Precision = TP/(TP+FP)
- Recall = TP/(TP+FN)
- F1 = 2*(Precision*Recall)/(Precision+Recall)","# Dataset Description

