10081,stat-5385-6385-project-1-2025,"# Overview

The goal of this competition is to estimate the growth of bacteria after some time has elapsed. The metric to evaluate the prediction is the square error.
----------------------
# Description

You are a **Data Scientist** in a biology lab. The lab conducts experiments on the *Paramecium* bacteria. They put a drop of fluid containing the bacteria in a *Petri* dish and let the bacteria grow. After a certain time, they conduct several test on the bacteria. They have conducted this type of experiment several times in the past and they have recorded the time (in days) that they have let the bacteria grow and what is the area that the bacteria covers in the *Petri* dish at the end of the growth period. So they have recorded several measurements of **Area** and **Days**. They will conduct new experiments and want you to predict the **Area** that the bacteria will cover after a certain amount of time. So they will provide you with the **Days** and want the prediction of the **Area**, based on previous measurements.

They know the model can't be too complicated and have told you, that no other variables are used. Furthermore, you can only use the following transformations (for the **Area** and/or for the **Days**):

* Square root: 
$$\sqrt{x}$$
* Square
$$x^2$$
* Natural Logarithm
$$\log{x}$$

Any combination of this function on the independent variable or dependent variable or both is allowed.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Your predictions will be scored using the [Mean Square Error](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_squared_error).

Your grade will be computed using the following formula:

$$\max\left(0, \left(2 - \frac{\text{Your Score}}{\text{Minimum Score}}\right) * 100\right)$$

## Submission File
For each ID in the test set, you must predict the **Area**. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    colID,AREA
    1,11
    2,23
    3,5
    etc.","# Dataset Description

You will be provided with individual data sets containing two variables:

* **Area**
* **Days**

The first column of the ""Comma Separated Values"" file is the **Area** and the second column is the **Days**.

This file is personalized for each student, and has the following naming structure:
""data_project_1_studentame.csv"". Your results should be based only in your data file. You will receive this file by email.

Here on Kaggle, you will find the test file, containing only the **Days**, variable that you will use to predict the **Area**. The file name is: ""test_data.csv"".",False,True
