# Evaluation


## Evaluation Protocol

### 1. Prediction Performance Score (60 %)

After prediction submission, the organizing committee will evaluate consistency between predicted results and ground-truth annotations. 
The predictive performance score is calculated by averaging the scores across 8 datasets.
Two evaluation metrics are used for these datasets:

- Average Accuracy: Mean annotation accuracy over test datasets 1¨C7:

$$S_{Accuracy}=\frac{N_{right}}{N_{all}}$$

where, $N_{right}$ denotes the number of correctly annotated samples, and $N_{all}$ denotes the total number of test samples.
- Consistency-Aware Metric£ºFor Test dataset 8, we adopt a consistency-aware metric based on code generation to assess the logical consistency of model outputs. This metric focuses on the alignment between executability and computational correctness of the generated code. Specifically, the generated code is required not only to execute successfully but also to produce correct computational results. The score is defined as follows:

$$S_{Consistency}=S_{Execution}(1-\frac{S_{Call}-S_{Execution}}{S_{Call}})$$

where, $S_{Call}$ denotes the proportion of generated code that can be successfully invoked and executed at the functional level, and $S_{Execution}$ denotes the proportion of generated code that correctly completes the computation and produces the expected results.

### 2. Technical Solution Score (40 %)

The organizing committee will reproduce submitted code and evaluate the technical solution in conjunction with the technical report, focusing on the depth and effectiveness of solutions to the following core challenges:

- Prompt and instruction design for stable, high-quality annotation in ultra-long contexts (20%)
- How to construct information-dense and structurally coherent ultra-long contexts when the number of available annotated examples significantly exceeds the model¡¯s context capacity (40%)
- Efficient utilization of ultra-long contexts in multi-turn or continuous annotation settings, balancing consistency and scalability (40%)

</br>
</br>

**Notes:**
- Solutions that cannot be successfully reproduced will be disqualified from final ranking.
- During the reproducibility phase, the organizing committee will deploy the Qwen3-4B in a unified hardware environment and conduct reproduction experiments on the solutions submitted by the participating teams.

