10103,ar-xiv-paper-topic-classification,"# Overview

?? ArXiv Paper Topic Classification Challenge

Welcome to the ArXiv Paper Topic Classification Challenge!

Every day, thousands of scientific papers are uploaded to arXiv.org
, covering fields from computer science to mathematics and physics. With such a vast amount of research, automatically classifying papers into their correct categories is an essential step for organizing knowledge and making it more discoverable.

In this competition, you will build machine learning models that can predict the research category of an academic paper based only on its metadata.

?? Goal

Your task is to predict the category label (label) of each paper in the test set, given the provided information.
This is a multi-class text classification problem, using the top-N most common arXiv categories (e.g., cs.CL, math.CO, physics.optics, etc.).

Participants will be ranked based on their model¡¯s performance on the hidden test set.
----------------------
# Description

?? Competition Description
Domain Background

arXiv.org
 is one of the world¡¯s largest open-access repositories of scientific papers, with millions of submissions spanning disciplines such as computer science, mathematics, physics, and beyond.
However, with the continuous growth of submissions, automated classification of research papers has become an important task to help researchers and librarians organize and retrieve knowledge efficiently.

Problem Statement

In this competition, your goal is to predict the research category of an arXiv paper given its metadata.

Each paper is represented by an ID and a label corresponding to its main subject category (e.g., cs.CL, math.CO, physics.optics, etc.).

This is a multi-class text classification problem, where your model must map each paper ID in the test set to its most likely research field.


----------------------
# Evaluation

Data Details

You will be working with four CSV files:

train.csv ¨C the training set containing id and label.

test.csv ¨C the test set containing only id (labels hidden).

submission.csv ¨C a sample submission file (id,label) in the correct format.

solution.csv ¨C hidden ground truth labels with Usage column (Public / Private) used for scoring.

Example Submission
id,label
1001,cs.CL
1002,math.CO
1003,physics.optics","# Dataset Description

