10151,ift-6390-ift-3395-beer-quality-prediction,"# Description

[English] 
This Kaggle competition is the first competition of the **IFT6390-IFT3395 course.** The goal is to get you familiar with simple algorithm for supervised learning. In this competition, you'll be working with **beer quality datasets.** Your goal is to analyze and preprocess the data, and create the best possible model to predict beer quality based on various bio-chemical features.

You will be given a Jupyter notebook with all the instructions. We suggest you work with this file; however, you're free to download the dataset yourself and work with any language you like as long as your submission follows the expected format. The dataset can be found in the Data tab. 

Your submission will be evaluated on the `test.csv` dataset, which has been split internally into two hidden groups:

- **Public leaderboard**: evaluated on the `public` portion of the test dataset. This leaderboard is available at any time during the competition and provides real-time relative ranking.

- **Private leaderboard** : evaluated on the `private` portion of the test dataset. This learderboard remains hidden until the end of the competition to ensure that final rankings reflect true generalization performance rather than overfitting to the available leaderboard.

The Leaderboard tab contains the public ranking of submissions.

You can make up to **3 submissions per day**, and you can choose 1 submission for the private ranking.

===============================================================================

