---

## ?? Overview

**VReID-XFD 2025** introduces the **first large-scale benchmark** for *video-based human recognition at extreme far distances (XFD)*.  
This challenge aims to evaluate models that can **recognize individuals across UAV (aerial) and ground cameras** under real-world conditions ¡ª including extreme variations in **scale, viewpoint, clothing, and illumination**.

?? **Official Workshop Website:** [https://www.it.ubi.pt/VReID-XFD/#intro](https://www.it.ubi.pt/VReID-XFD/#intro)

---

## ?? Challenge Tracks

| Track | Description |
|:------|:-------------|
| **A¡úG** | Match aerial to ground-view videos |
| **G¡úA** | Retrieve aerial identities from ground inputs |
| **A¡úA** | Match subjects across aerial videos |

Each track evaluates **cross-view** and **cross-session** generalization performance.





---

## ??? Dataset Highlights

- **553 unique identities** recorded over **two sessions per subject**  
- **13M+ annotated bounding boxes** in video format  
- **16 soft-biometric attributes** (clothing color, hairstyle, accessories, etc.)  
