10243,the-3lc-cotton-weed-detection-challenge,"# Overview

# ?? Cotton Weed Detection Challenge  

**Welcome to agricultural AI that mirrors real-world data and model-building challenges!**  

Build an accurate weed detection model under **real constraints** of small models and imperfect labels - the kind of conditions production AI teams face every day.  

### ?? The Challenge

**Target Species:** Detect and classify **3 types of problematic weeds** in cotton field imagery:
- **Class 0: Carpetweed** - Mat-forming competitor
- **Class 1: Morning Glory** - Climbing vine causing major yield losses  
- **Class 2: Palmer Amaranth** - Herbicide-resistant ""super weed""

**Model Constraint:** Use the **YOLOv8n** model with **640 image input size**. You may tune augmentation and hyperparameters, but no larger models, ensembles, or stacking allowed. The fixed model mirrors deployment scenarios where compute and memory budgets are absolute.

**Data Reality:** The dataset includes **labeling imperfections** - missed weeds, confused classes, and inconsistent bounding boxes. This isn't accidental; it reflects what happens when data is labeled by groups of annotators. Even with clear instructions, variability in interpretation, annotator fatigue, and differences in expertise lead to mistakes. For production AI teams, this is the rule rather than the exception - and success comes from learning to detect, adapt, and improve around these issues systematically.  

**The Solution:** Master data-centric AI techniques using [3LC](https://3lc.ai/) to achieve maximum performance within these real-world constraints.

### What Makes This Different

- **Traditional Kaggle Approach:** Scale up models, blend ensembles, or use post-processing tricks to chase leaderboard points - often without ever touching the data.  
- **Production AI Reality:** You can't ensemble your way around hardware and cost limits. Real gains come from **working within fixed constraints, systematically improving the data**, and then refining training.  

In production, teams increasingly rely on feedback from the model itself to improve labels and datasets - not just once, but through an **iterative loop: train, fix the data, then retrain.** This cycle, at the heart of [3LC](https://3lc.ai/), is what this competition encourages: continuously refine the data as you train, not just the model.  

### ?? Prizes & Recognition

**Total Prize Pool: $2,000 USD**

| Place | Prize | Recognition |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| ?? **1st Place** | **$1,000** | Winner Certificate + LinkedIn Feature |
| ?? **2nd Place** | **$500** | Second Place Certificate + LinkedIn Feature |
| ?? **3rd Place** | **$250** | Third Place Certificate + LinkedIn Feature |
| ?? **Most Innovative** | **$250** | Up to 5 teams share ($50 each) |

**Recognition Awards:**
- ?? **Ranks 1-3:** Winner certificates + LinkedIn/community features
- ?? **Ranks 4-15:** Participation certificates + community recognition

### ?? Competition Timeline

- **Duration:** 1.5 Months  
- **Team Limit:** 3 participants per team at max
- **Dataset:** 542 training + 133 validation + 170 test images
- **Submissions:** 3 per day maximum
- **Final Selection:** Choose up to 2 submissions for final judging

### ?? What You'll Learn

**Industry-Relevant Skills:**  
- Developing AI under **strict resource constraints**  
- Applying **data-centric techniques** to detect and correct label issues  
- Setting up an **iterative train¨Cfix¨Cretrain loop** guided by model feedback  
- Designing pipelines that **scale from experimentation to production**  

**Why This Matters:**  
In production AI, constraints aren't optional - they're reality. This challenge trains you to think beyond brute force and build smarter, leaner, data-driven solutions.

### ?? Requirements

#### Hardware & Software

**Operating System:**
- Windows 10 or 11 (x86)
- macOS Ventura (version 13) or newer (Apple Silicon M-series ARM only)
- Ubuntu 20.04 or newer (x86-64)

**Python Environment:**
- Python 3.9, 3.10, or 3.11
- PyTorch and Torchvision 1.9+
- **GPU strongly recommended** - [Install CUDA-enabled PyTorch](https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/)

**3LC Dashboard:**
- Chrome or Edge browser with GPU acceleration enabled
- Check: `chrome://gpu` or `edge://gpu` ¡ú WebGL should be ""Hardware accelerated""

**Recommended Setup:**
- Discrete GPU (NVIDIA/AMD)
- 8GB+ RAM
- 50GB+ free disk space

#### Why Not Google Colab?  

**3LC Service Requirement**  
The 3LC Dashboard depends on a locally running service (`3lc service`) that opens a port on `localhost`. This enables you to use the 3LC Dashboard UI in your browser to explore tables and detailed per-sample metrics from your run, and make dataset revisions. Because Colab runs in a remote, ephemeral environment, this setup isn¡¯t supported there.  

**Recommendation**  
For the best experience, run on a local machine or cloud node with a GPU. This way, you can keep the 3LC service running continuously and take full advantage of the interactive dashboard.  

### ?? Getting Started

1. **Download the dataset** from the Data tab
2. **Set up 3LC:**
   - Create free account: [https://account.3lc.ai](https://account.3lc.ai)
   - Follow setup in the starter notebook
3. **Open:** `cotton_weed_starter_notebook.ipynb`
4. **Follow the workflow:**
   - Register dataset as 3LC Tables
   - Train baseline YOLOv8n model
   - Analyze errors in 3LC Dashboard
   - Generate predictions and submit CSV
5. **Join the community:** [Discord Server](https://discord.gg/T6GS5nWGp8) for questions and discussions

**New to object detection?** No problem! The starter notebook provides a complete workflow.

### ?? Resources & Support

- **3LC Platform:** [https://3lc.ai/](https://3lc.ai/)
- **3LC LinkedIN:** [https://www.linkedin.com/company/3lc-ai/posts/?feedView=all](https://www.linkedin.com/company/3lc-ai/posts/?feedView=all)
- **3LC Documentation:** [https://docs.3lc.ai/](https://docs.3lc.ai/)
- **Community Discord:** [https://discord.gg/T6GS5nWGp8](https://discord.gg/T6GS5nWGp8)
- **Competition Discussion:** Kaggle discussion forums
- **Technical Support:** Post in Discord or discussion tab

**Ready to tackle real-world agricultural AI?** Let's begin! ??
----------------------
# Description

## Edge AI in Agricultural Production

### Why This Matters
Precision weed detection can reduce herbicide usage by up to 80% compared to traditional broadcast spraying, targeting only areas with actual weed presence while maintaining crop protection effectiveness.

### The Technical Reality
Edge devices bring strict limitations: constrained processing power, fixed memory budgets, and limited energy use. These restrictions mean you can't simply scale up to larger models. For this challenge, the edge device is optimized for **YOLOv8n**, with input size fixed at **640**.  

## Why Data-Centric AI?

**The Traditional Approach Fails:**
- Can't use bigger models (hardware won't support them)
- Can't add more compute (power budget is fixed)  
- Can't upgrade infrastructure (economically infeasible)

**The Data-Centric Solution:**
When the model can't grow, the data must improve. This competition emphasizes the **train¨Cfix¨Cretrain loop** guided by model feedback using **3LC** - the real-world workflow behind production AI:  
- **Systematic data quality improvement** (fixing inconsistent or missing labels)  
- **Strategic data augmentation** to stretch model capacity  
- **Iterative error analysis and relabeling** to surface and correct dataset flaws  
- **Professional experiment tracking** for reproducible improvements  

**Learn more:** [3LC Platform](https://3lc.ai/) | [Documentation](https://docs.3lc.ai/)

**Model Constraints:**
- **Allowed:** YOLOv8n ONLY
- **Input Size:** 640 (fixed)
- **Prohibited:** YOLOv8s, YOLOv8m, YOLOv8l, YOLOv8x, and all other architectures
- **Reasoning:** Reflects the strictest edge device constraints in agricultural robotics

**You May Optimize:**
- Hyperparameters (learning rate, batch size, epochs)
- Training augmentation (mosaic, mixup, rotation, etc.)
- Data quality improvements using 3LC
- Confidence thresholds

## ?? Target Species

### Class 0: Carpetweed (*Mollugo verticillata*)
- **Growth:** Mat-forming annual
- **Visual ID:** Small white flowers, whorled leaves
- **Challenge:** Small size, blends with soil

### Class 1: Morning Glory (*Ipomoea species*)
- **Growth:** Vigorous climbing vine
- **Visual ID:** Heart-shaped leaves, trumpet flowers
- **Challenge:** Complex bounding boxes

### Class 2: Palmer Amaranth (*Amaranthus palmeri*)
- **Growth:** Fast-growing upright (6-8 feet)
- **Visual ID:** Lance-shaped leaves
- **Challenge:** Resembles cotton seedlings early

## ?? Data Quality Challenges

Your dataset reflects real-world messiness:  
- **Label Variability:** Mislabels, missed weeds, inconsistent bounding boxes
- **Environmental Factors:** Lighting changes, occlusions, soil variations

Production AI reality: labels are never perfect. [3LC](https://3lc.ai/) helps you systematically improve them.

## ?? Competition Success Strategy

**Phase 1:** Register data as [3LC Tables](https://docs.3lc.ai/)  
**Phase 2:** Train baseline YOLOv8n, submit to Kaggle  
**Phase 3:** Analyze errors in 3LC Dashboard, apply train¨Cfix¨Cretrain loop  
**Phase 4:** Advanced techniques (augmentation, reweighting, embeddings)

**Need help?** Join our [Discord community](https://discord.gg/T6GS5nWGp8) for support and discussions! ??
----------------------
# Evaluation

## ?? Submission Format

Upload a CSV file with exactly these columns (lowercase, case-sensitive):
```csv
image_id,prediction_string
20190613_6062W_CM_29,""0 0.85 0.5 0.3 0.2 0.4 1 0.72 0.7 0.6 0.15 0.25""
20200612_iPhone6_B_2,""2 0.91 0.4 0.6 0.3 0.4""  
20200624_iPhone6_SY_132,""no box""
```

?? **Important:** Column names must be lowercase: `image_id` and `prediction_string`

## ?? Prediction String Format

Each detection contains **6 space-separated values**:

```
class_id confidence x_center y_center width height
```

**Requirements:**
- **class_id**: Must be 0, 1, or 2 (corresponding to the 3 weed classes)
- **confidence**: Model confidence score (0.0 to 1.0)
- **x_center, y_center, width, height**: Normalized coordinates (0.0 to 1.0)
- **Multiple detections**: Concatenate all predictions with spaces
- **No detections**: Use `""no box""`

## ?? Evaluation Metric

**mAP@0.5** (Mean Average Precision at IoU = 0.5)
- Based on the COCO evaluation framework, restricted to a single IoU threshold (0.5).
- Measures detection accuracy with moderate localization quality requirements.
- Equal weighting across all 3 weed classes.
- **Perfect Score:** 1.0 | **Baseline:** ~0.30-0.40

### How mAP@0.5 Works
1. **IoU Calculation:** For each prediction, compute Intersection over Union with each ground truth box
2. **Matching:** A prediction with IoU ¡Ý 0.5 can match one ground truth (best match chosen). Extra predictions count as false positives
3. **Precision/Recall:** Compute precision and recall over all confidence thresholds
4. **Average Precision:** The area under the precision¨Crecall curve for each class
5. **Mean AP:** The average of AP values across the 3 classes

## ?? Leaderboard Structure

- **Public:** 50% of test (85 images) - immediate feedback
- **Private:** 50% of test (85 images) - determines final rankings
- **Submissions:** 3 per day max, select 2 final

## ?? Submission Requirements

**For All Participants:**
- Valid CSV format
- Normalized coordinates [0,1]
- YOLOv8n model only

**For Prize Winners:** Final evaluation steps announced in last competition week

## ?? Creative Solution Award

Innovative [3LC](https://3lc.ai/) usage demonstrating:
- Novel data analysis techniques
- Creative train-fix-retrain workflows
- Systematic improvement through model feedback

Up to 5 teams share $250 ($50 each)

## ?? Important Notes

**Format:** Use starter notebook for auto-generated correct CSV  
**Model:** ONLY YOLOv8n permitted  
**Support:** Questions? Join [Discord](https://discord.gg/T6GS5nWGp8) or post in discussions

Good luck! ??
