# Evaluation

## Evaluation

Submissions will be evaluated using [Mean Absolute Error (MAE)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_absolute_error),

![MAE](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/visipedia/iwildcam_comp/master/assets/MAE.png)

where each `x_i` represents the predicted target, `y_i` represents the ground truth, and `n` is the number of rows in the test set.

## Submission File
For each `id` in the test set, you must predict the target `yield`. The file should contain a header and have the following format:

    id,yield
    15289,6025.194
    15290,1256.223
    15291,357.44
    etc.",,False,True
10258,dl-2025-project-2,"# Overview

Your task is to perform a binary classification and detect whether there is a crack or not. This version of the project is the simplest and therefore can be awarded with a grade of 3.0 at most.
Besides high accuracy, it is also important to perform all important steps of the neural network creation and training like data preprocessing, architecture selection, results analysis.

Use the following dataset https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/lakshaymiddha/crack-segmentation-dataset. Only the train directory is supposed to be used during the training.","# Dataset Description

