## Columns

## Dataset Columns and Descriptions

- `Date` ¡ª The corresponding trading date for the record. Each date acts as a unique identifier for the stock data entry (example_id).  
- `Open` ¡ª The stock price at the beginning of the trading session. This represents the first price at which the stock was traded when the market opened. **(target variable)**
- `High` ¡ª The highest price reached by the stock during the trading day.  
- `Low` ¡ª The lowest price reached by the stock during the trading day.  
- `Close` ¡ª The final price of the stock at the end of the trading day.**(target variable - you will model the time series using this feature)**
- `Volume` ¡ª The total number of shares traded during that day. It reflects the liquidity and activity level of the stock.  
- `Dividends` ¡ª The cash amount per share distributed to shareholders on that date. It represents the portion of a company¡¯s earnings paid out to investors.  
- `StockSplits` ¡ª Indicates any stock split that occurred on that date. For example, a 2-for-1 split means every share was split into two, halving the price per share.  
- `Company` ¡ª The name of the company.
- `Inflation` ¡ª The inflation rate or inflation-related indicator corresponding to the same period.",False,True
