10439,mds-datathon,"# Overview

#?? Can You Predict the Next Tsunami?
Welcome to the MDS Tsunami Datathon! This competition challenges you to build a machine learning model that predicts whether an earthquake will trigger a tsunami based on seismic characteristics.

#?? Competition Overview
Tsunamis are devastating natural disasters that can cause massive loss of life and infrastructure damage. Early warning systems are critical for coastal communities, but predicting which earthquakes will generate tsunamis remains challenging. Your task is to analyze historical earthquake data and build a classifier that can accurately identify tsunami-generating events.

##The Challenge
Using seismic features such as magnitude, depth, location, and intensity measurements, predict whether an earthquake event resulted in a tsunami (binary classification: 0 = No Tsunami, 1 = Tsunami).

##Why This Matters
Lives Saved: Accurate predictions enable faster evacuations
Infrastructure Protection: Better warning systems reduce economic impact
Scientific Advancement: Improve our understanding of tsunami-generating mechanisms
Real-World Impact: Your models could inform future early warning systems
----------------------
# Evaluation

#Metric
Accuracy Score - Percentage of correct tsunami predictions

Your submissions will be evaluated on classification accuracy. The public leaderboard shows your performance on 50% of the test data during the competition. Final rankings are determined by the private leaderboard (remaining 50%).


## Submission File
Submission Format

Submit a CSV file with two columns:

```csv
id,tsunami
0,1
1,0
2,1
```",,False,True
