## ?? Data Format
Data generated on FalconCloud will have this format:

### 1. **Images**  
- Format: `.jpg` , `.png`
- Dimensions: All synthetic images created on FalconCloud will be `1920x1080px`.  

### 2. **Labels (YOLO Format)**  
Each image has a corresponding `.txt` file with annotations:  
class_id x_center y_center width height

- Values are **normalized** (0-1) relative to image dimensions  
- Example (`0001.txt`):  
0 0.45 0.50 0.20 0.15 # building


### 3. **Class ID**  
- Only **class 0**: building (vehicle annotations will be present but not scored)

---

## ?? What You're Predicting
Predict **bounding boxes** for real-world test images in YOLO format:  
- csv file of all predictions with 2 major entries being, ""image_id"", ""prediction_string""  
- Each line: `image_id"", "" object_class confidence x_center y_center width height""`  
- **Confidence scores** must be between 0 and 1

---

## ?? Acronyms
| Term | Definition |  
|------|------------|  
| **YOLO** | You Only Look Once (object detection architecture) |  
| **mAP@50** | Mean Average Precision at 50% IoU |  
| **IoU** | Intersection over Union (box overlap metric) |  

---

