10515,Soil-moisture-inversion-using-GNSS-R-methods,"# Overview

# GNSS-R Soil Moisture Retrieval Challenge

**Advancing Global Soil Moisture Monitoring with Spaceborne GNSS Reflectometry**

## Competition Summary
This competition leverages publicly available GNSS-Reflectometry (GNSS-R) data from NASA's CYGNSS (Cyclone Global Navigation Satellite System) constellation (2017¨C2024) to push the boundaries of high-accuracy soil moisture retrieval using reflected satellite signals.

Participants will predict **volumetric surface soil moisture (0¨C5 cm depth, in cm3/cm3)** from GNSS-R reflectivity measurements and auxiliary features, addressing real-world challenges like vegetation cover, surface roughness, topography, and radio-frequency interference.

The dataset includes over 50 million high-quality samples across global land surfaces, with ground truth co-located from the International Soil Moisture Network (ISMN) in-situ stations and/or SMAP/SMOS satellite products.

## Task
- **Type**: Regression
- Predict soil moisture for each row in the test set.
- Submission format: CSV with columns `id` (or row index) and `soil_moisture`.

## Why Participate?
GNSS-R offers unique advantages: all-weather observations, high spatio-temporal density (~1¨C10 km daily in mid/low latitudes), and low-cost scalability compared to traditional microwave missions (e.g., SMAP at ~36 km).

Winning models could enable operational global soil moisture products, benefiting:
- Agricultural drought monitoring
- Hydrological forecasting
- Climate modeling and land-atmosphere interactions

## Dataset Highlights
- **Features**: Reflectivity (¦£), incidence/azimuth angles, coherence, surface roughness, vegetation opacity (¦Ó), NDVI, elevation (DEM), land cover, time-series statistics, etc.
- **Scale**: ~45M training rows, ~5¨C10M test rows
- **Challenges**: Heterogeneous surfaces, seasonal variations, frozen soil, RFI

Join us to innovate in remote sensing and machine learning for Earth observation!

**Acknowledgments**  
Data provided by NASA CYGNSS mission (PO.DAAC), ISMN, and SMAP/SMOS teams.
----------------------
# Description

# GNSS-R Soil Moisture Retrieval Challenge

**Advancing Global Soil Moisture Monitoring with Spaceborne GNSS Reflectometry**

## Competition Summary
This competition leverages publicly available GNSS-Reflectometry (GNSS-R) data from NASA's CYGNSS (Cyclone Global Navigation Satellite System) constellation (2017¨C2024) to push the boundaries of high-accuracy soil moisture retrieval using reflected satellite signals.

Participants will predict **volumetric surface soil moisture (0¨C5 cm depth, in cm3/cm3)** from GNSS-R reflectivity measurements and auxiliary features, addressing real-world challenges like vegetation cover, surface roughness, topography, and radio-frequency interference.

The dataset includes over 50 million high-quality samples across global land surfaces, with ground truth co-located from the International Soil Moisture Network (ISMN) in-situ stations and/or SMAP/SMOS satellite products.

## Task
- **Type**: Regression
- Predict soil moisture for each row in the test set.
- Submission format: CSV with columns `id` (or row index) and `soil_moisture`.

## Why Participate?
GNSS-R offers unique advantages: all-weather observations, high spatio-temporal density (~1¨C10 km daily in mid/low latitudes), and low-cost scalability compared to traditional microwave missions (e.g., SMAP at ~36 km).

Winning models could enable operational global soil moisture products, benefiting:
- Agricultural drought monitoring
- Hydrological forecasting
- Climate modeling and land-atmosphere interactions

## Dataset Highlights
- **Features**: Reflectivity (¦£), incidence/azimuth angles, coherence, surface roughness, vegetation opacity (¦Ó), NDVI, elevation (DEM), land cover, time-series statistics, etc.
- **Scale**: ~45M training rows, ~5¨C10M test rows
- **Challenges**: Heterogeneous surfaces, seasonal variations, frozen soil, RFI

Join us to innovate in remote sensing and machine learning for Earth observation!

**Acknowledgments**  
Data provided by NASA CYGNSS mission (PO.DAAC), ISMN, and SMAP/SMOS teams.
----------------------
# Evaluation

# Evaluation

## Metric
Submissions are evaluated using **unbiased Root Mean Square Difference (ubRMSD)** as the primary metric:

$$
\text{ubRMSD} = \sqrt{\frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^{n} ((\hat{y}_i - \mu_{\hat{y}}) - (y_i - \mu_y))^2}
$$

where:
- $\hat{y}_i$: predicted soil moisture
- $y_i$: ground truth soil moisture
- $\mu_{\hat{y}}$ and $\mu_y$: means of predictions and truth (removed to eliminate bias)

Lower ubRMSD is better. Typical targets: < 0.04 cm3/cm3 for state-of-the-art.

## Secondary Metrics (for reference)
- RMSE: $\sqrt{\frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^{n} (\hat{y}_i - y_i)^2}$
- Bias: $\frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^{n} (\hat{y}_i - y_i)$
- Pearson correlation coefficient (R)

## Leaderboard
- **Public Leaderboard**: Scored on ~30% of the private test set (visible during competition).
- **Private Leaderboard**: Scored on the remaining ~70% (final rankings, revealed at end to prevent overfitting).
- Final ranking based solely on private ubRMSD.
- Teams may select up to 2 submissions for final scoring.

## Additional Notes
- The test set covers similar temporal/spatial distribution as training but includes unseen regions/seasons.
- NaN predictions are not allowed; invalid submissions score infinitely.","# Dataset Description

# Data

## Files
- **train.csv** (~45 million rows): Training data with features and target soil moisture values.
- **test.csv** (~5¨C10 million rows): Test data for predictions (target is hidden).
- **sample_submission.csv**: Example submission file format.

All files are in CSV format. Rows represent individual GNSS-R measurement samples (point observations over land).

**Note**: Data is large-scale tabular. Use efficient libraries like Pandas with chunking or Dask for loading. Expect some NaN values due to real-world measurement gaps (e.g., RFI flags or missing auxiliary data).

## Columns (Features and Target)

| Column Name              | Type    | Description                                                                 | Units / Notes |
|--------------------------|---------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------|
| id                       | int     | Unique row identifier (for submission matching in test.csv)                | - |
| lat                      | float   | Latitude of the specular reflection point                                  | Degrees (-90 to 90) |
| lon                      | float   | Longitude of the specular reflection point                                 | Degrees (-180 to 180) |
| time                     | datetime| Observation timestamp (UTC)                                                 | YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS |
| reflectivity             | float   | GNSS-R surface reflectivity (¦£, normalized power)                          | Unitless (typically 0¨C30 dB) |
| incidence_angle          | float   | Satellite incidence (elevation) angle                                       | Degrees (0¨C90) |
| azimuth_angle            | float   | Azimuth angle relative to track                                            | Degrees |
| coherence                | float   | Signal coherence (indicator of specular vs. diffuse reflection)            | Unitless (0¨C1) |
| surface_roughness        | float   | Estimated surface roughness parameter                                      | meters or unitless |
| vegetation_opacity       | float   | Vegetation optical depth (¦Ó) at L-band                                     | Unitless (nepers) |
| ndvi                     | float   | Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (auxiliary, from MODIS/AVHRR)      | -1 to 1 |
| elevation                | float   | Surface elevation from DEM (e.g., SRTM)                                    | meters |
| land_cover               | int     | Land cover class (e.g., IGBP classification: 1=Evergreen Forest, etc.)     | Integer code |
| rfi_flag                 | bool/int| Radio Frequency Interference flag (1 = contaminated, recommend filtering) | 0/1 |
| ... (additional features)| ...     | Time-series stats (e.g., mean reflectivity last 7 days), etc.              | Varies |
| soil_moisture (target)   | float   | Volumetric soil moisture (0¨C5 cm depth) **Only in train.csv**              | cm3/cm3 (0¨C1 typical range) |

## Additional Notes
- **Target Distribution**: Soil moisture values range from ~0.0 (dry) to ~0.6 cm3/cm3 (saturated), with regional/seasonal variations. Expect skewness in arid vs. humid areas.
- **Spatial/Temporal Coverage**: Primarily ¡À38¡ã latitude (CYGNSS orbit), 2017¨C2024, global land (filtered ocean/coast).
- **Challenges**: High heterogeneity (vegetation, topography, frozen soil in winter). NaNs common in auxiliary features¡ªimpute or mask as needed.
- **Ground Truth**: Target derived from co-located ISMN in-situ measurements and/or SMAP/SMOS products (nearest-neighbor matching with quality filters).
- **Recommended Baseline**: Start with simple models (e.g., LightGBM) on raw features, then add time-series engineering.

Download and explore in a Kaggle Notebook for fast iteration!

**Data Sources Acknowledgment**  
Based on NASA CYGNSS L3 products, ISMN, SMAP ancillary data. For full citations, see Overview page.",False,True
