10519,manthan-ai-2025-ai-summit,"# Overview

Hackathon Overview (Corrected & Professional Version)

Participants will be provided with three problem statements. You must choose one of them, analyze it thoroughly, and use the given dataset to train a machine learning model. After building the model, integrate it into a real-life use case and present it in the form of an app, dashboard, website, or any functional application.

Alternatively, you may select the Open Innovation track, where you are free to choose any relevant dataset and build an impactful real-world solution.

Your project will be evaluated based on the following criteria:

Model performance and accuracy

Quality of analysis and understanding of the problem

Practicality and innovation of the real-life use case

User interface and overall presentation during the demo

How useful your solution is as a real product

Make sure your final submission is well-structured, functional, and clearly demonstrates how your model solves the chosen problem.
----------------------
# Description

This hackathon challenges participants to transform data into meaningful, real-world solutions. You will be provided with three carefully designed problem statements, each containing a dataset. Your task is to choose one problem, perform a complete analysis, build a machine learning model, and integrate it into a functional application such as an app, dashboard, or website.

For teams opting for Open Innovation, you may bring your own dataset and develop any innovative project that addresses a real-world need.

The goal of this hackathon is not only to test your technical skills but also to evaluate how effectively you can convert your model into a useful, practical product.

Judging will be based on:

Depth of problem understanding and EDA

Model accuracy and reliability

Creativity and relevance of your real-life use case

Design, usability, and overall presentation of your solution

Product impact and scalability

This is your opportunity to showcase your ability to turn raw data into a powerful, impactful solution that solves real problems.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Evaluation Criteria

Projects will be evaluated by the judges based on the following key parameters:

1. Problem Understanding & EDA

Clarity in understanding the selected problem statement

Quality of Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

Insights extracted from the data

Clear explanation of findings and approach

2. Model Development & Performance

Choice of algorithms and justification

Preprocessing, feature engineering, and experimentation

Model accuracy, precision/recall, or other relevant metrics

Efficiency and robustness of the final model

3. Real-Life Use Case Integration

How well the model fits into a real-world application

Practicality, usefulness, and innovation of the solution

Clear demonstration of how the model solves the problem

4. Application/UI/UX

Quality of the app, dashboard, or website

Ease of use, clean design, and good user experience

Functionality and smooth execution during the demo

5. Presentation & Communication

Clarity in explaining the workflow, logic, and results

Ability to answer judges¡¯ questions

Storytelling and showcasing the product¡¯s value

6. Product Impact & Scalability

Potential impact of the solution in real life

Uniqueness and creativity

Scalability and future improvement scope",,False,True
