----------------------
# CVPR26 and CLEF26 Context

This competition is held jointly as part of:

* the [LifeCLEF 2026 lab](https://www.imageclef.org/LifeCLEF2026) of the [CLEF 2026](https://clef2026.clef-initiative.eu/) conference, and of
* the [FGVC13 workshop](https://sites.google.com/view/fgvc13/home) organized in conjunction with the [CVPR 2026 conference](https://cvpr.thecvf.com/).

Being part of scientific research, the participants are encouraged to participate to both events. In particular, only participants who submitted a working note paper to LifeCLEF (see below) will be part of the officially published ranking used for scientific communication.

### FGVC13 at CVPR 2026
This competition is part of the 13th Fine-Grained Visual Categorization (FGVC13) workshop in June at the Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Conference CVPR 2026. The task results will be presented at the workshop, and the contribution of the winning team(s) will be highlighted. Attending the workshop is not required to participate in the competition.

**CVPR 2026** will take place in **Denver, Colorado, USA, on June 3-7, 2026**.

**PLEASE NOTE:** CVPR frequently sells out early; we cannot guarantee CVPR registration after the competition's end. If you are interested in attending, please plan ahead.

You can see a list of the FGVC competitions [here](https://sites.google.com/view/fgvc13/competitions).

### LifeCLEF 2026 at CLEF 2026
LifeCLEF lab is part of the Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum (CLEF).
CLEF consists of independent peer-reviewed workshops on a broad range of challenges in multilingual and multimodal information access evaluation and benchmarking activities in various labs designed to test different aspects of mono and cross-language Information retrieval systems.

**CLEF 2026** will take place in **Jena, Germany, on September 21-24, 2026**.

You can find more details on the [CLEF 2026 website](https://clef2026.clef-initiative.eu/).
