10573,iaio-2026-selections-for-russia,"# Overview

This competitions will be a selection that defines a team of students who will represent Russia at IAIO 2026. The problems will cover a wide range of AI topics, including different domains in machine learning and math, testing students¡¯ practical and theoretical abilities. 

## Dates and Format:
**Dates:** Dec 6¨C9, 2025<br>

**Format:** Online participation with proctoring
<br>
## Competition Structure:  
**Dec 6** ¨C Two ML tasks<br>
**Dec 7** - Two ML tasks<br>
**Dec 8** - Math tasks<br>
**Dec 9** - English interview<br>

We like open competitions and selections, so these competitions are open to anyone - you can participate if you're not eligible (like if you're studying in university or you're not from Russia). **But note that to participate for team selection you have to register at https://form.centraluniversity.ru/IAIO_wait_list/ before December 5th 18:00 MSK**.

Tasks will be gradually released according to the following schedule:  

| Task   | Available From      | Available Until     | Link                       |
|--------|---------------------|---------------------|----------------------------|
| ML Task 1 | Dec 6, 09:00 MSK    | Dec 6, 11:00 MSK    | https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-sfr-timeseries-classification |
| ML Task 2 | Dec 6, 11:30 MSK    | Dec 6, 15:30 MSK    | https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-sf-r-recommend-music |
| ML Task 3 | Dec 7, 09:00 MSK    | Dec 7, 12:00 MSK    | https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-sf-r-comments-classification  |
| ML Task 4 | Dec 7, 13:00 MSK    | Dec 7, 17:00 MSK    | https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-sf-r-image-classification |
| Math tasks part 1 | Dec 8, 09:00 MSK    | Dec 8, 11:00 MSK    |  |
| Math tasks part 2 | Dec 8, 12:00 MSK    | Dec 8, 14:00 MSK    |  |

## Rules
Carefully read ""Rules"" section before joining the competitions.","# Dataset Description

This a test competition to help you familiarize yourself with Kaggle platform. Links to real competitions will be published in time in ""Overview"" tab of the page.

The data is quite simple: you have a set of images in `test` folder that you need to classify into 6 classes. In `train` folder there are certain examples of each class. Read ""Rules"" tab to learn more about NEOAI rules - they're going to be the same (minor changes are possible) for the rest 8 competitions you're going to participate in.

You need to write your predictions into `sample_submission.csv` file and submit it on Kaggle.

**Note that this is a competition where you have a small amount of samples and you can get the ideal accuracy of 1. Try to achieve that in the least amount of submissions possible! This is the real challenge here.**

We suggest you to use Kaggle notebooks which you can create in the ""Code"" tab.",False,True
