10613,solidworks-ai-hackathon,"# Overview

SOLIDWORKS AI Hackathon 

Welcome to the SOLIDWORKS AI Hackathon, hosted at IIT Madras!
Your mission in this competition is to build a machine learning model that can correctly identify which mechanical parts appear in a synthetic image.

Each image may contain a combination of:
- Bolt
- Locating Pin
- Nut
- Washer
----------------------
# Description

In this competition, you¡¯ll work with synthetic images containing common mechanical parts: bolts, locating pins, nuts, and washers. Each image may contain any combination of these four components.

Your goal is to build a model that predicts how many parts are present in each image.

You are provided with training images, test images, and a label file showing the part counts for each training image. During evaluation, these counts are treated as presence/absence.

Submit your predictions in the format:

image_name,bolt,locatingpin,nut,washer

where each value is number of the specified part
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated using exact-match accuracy.
For each test image, you must predict the number of parts present in an image . A prediction is counted as correct only if all four values match exactly.

The four part types, in order, are:
bolt
locatingpin
nut
washer


Submission File : 
Your submission must be a CSV file with the following columns:
image_name,bolt,locatingpin,nut,washer

Each value should be number of occurrences of the object in the image.

Example:
image_name,bolt,locatingpin,nut,washer
abc.png,1,0,2,0
xyz.png,0,1,0,3


Files not following this structure may result in a score of 0 or a submission error.","# Dataset Description

