10616,private-extract-container-numbers-from-bill-of-lading,"# Overview

This competition challenges participants to develop models capable of extracting container numbers from scanned bills of lading. The task focuses on information extraction from semi-structured documents where container identifiers appear in various layouts, fonts, and noise conditions.


----------------------
# Description

**Problem Statement:**
Given an image of a bill of lading, participants must identify and extract all container numbers present in the document. Container numbers follow a standard format but may appear in different positions or be partially degraded due to scanning.



----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation section describes how submissions will be scored and how participants should format their submissions. 

Submissions are evaluated on between the extracted containers and the actual containers present.
The evaluation metric penalizes both missing container numbers and incorrectly predicted container numbers. The score is computed independently for each document and then averaged across all documents.

The document-level score is defined as:

score_doc = 1 / (1 + n_wrong + n_missing)

The final competition score is the mean of score_doc over all documents. A perfect extraction yields a score of 1.0, while missing or incorrect extractions reduce the score proportionally.

## Submission File
For each ID (defined as below) in the test set, you must extract the containers numbers contained in the bill of lading. The file should contain a header and have the following format. You can find the file in the zip sent to you:

```python
id,container_numbers
CACAO FEVES/IGNIAZIO MESSINA/GHANA/BL TE4034594,LKU345645 MLLK445680 LMCU9104232
CACAO FEVES/GOLD STAR LINE LTD/GHANA/BL GOSUTEM8001586,ZCSU456643 ZCSU344443 ZCSU345555
CACAO FEVES/GOLD STAR LINE LTD/GHANA/BL GOSUTEM8001576,GAOU34555 JXLU345555
CACAO FEVES/ARKAS/GHANA/BL TMA000000062,ARKU654322 RFCU654333
...
```","# Dataset Description

Data will be shared with you via email.

