10617,query-intent-detection,"# Description

A customer service chatbot needs to detect the intent of user queries in order to provide appropriate suggestions and carry out appropriate actions for the customer. Specifically, it needs an automated system to evaluate whether the customer is requesting with an intent of one of the following categories:

- balance
- freeze_account
- pay_bill
- report_lost_card
- transactions
- transfer

And also detect whether the query is out of scope (not in these 6 categories, AND not in other intents that the customer service chatbot is designed to cover). Out-of-scope requests may involve those requiring hardware action, related to subjective opinions, or related to sensitive yet safety-critical domains.

Your job is to develop the core of that automated system. Using NLP techniques, detect whether the user query corresponds to any of the intents described above.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions are evaluated on a custom weighted F1 score that is a weighted average of F1 scores across the target categories:
- 1/12 for each of balance, freeze_account, pay_bill, report_lost_card, transactions, transfer
- 1/2 for out-of-scope

For example, if the F1 scores are:
- 0.8 for balance
- 0.9 for freeze_account
- 0.9 for pay_bill
- 0.8 for report_lost_card
- 0.9 for transactions
- 0.8 for transfer
- 0.6 for out-of-scope

Then the weighted F1 score on the leaderboard will be:
- 0.8 * 1/12 + 0.9 * 1/12 + 0.9 * 1/12 + 0.8 * 1/12 + 0.9 * 1/12 + 0.8 * 1/12 + 0.6 * 1/2 = 0.725

## Submission File
For each id in the test set, you must predict the value of the label variable, which is the intent that the query corresponds to. The file should contain a header and have the following format below. See the baseline code for more details.

    id,label
    0,other
    1,other
    2,out-of-scope
    etc.",,False,True
