10624,the-blind-flight-synapse-drive-ps-1,"# Overview

<section id=""ps1-overview"">
  <h2>Problem Statement 1 ¨C Visual Navigation & Path Planning</h2>

  <p>
    Several Stark navigation systems are currently offline. The autonomous flight stack has lost its high-level logic and
    needs to be rebuilt from scratch. Your job in this problem statement is to take noisy visual inputs and reconstruct a
    usable navigation representation, then compute an efficient path across the map under a cost function that depends on
    terrain and local ¡°velocity¡± boosts.
  </p>

  <h3>Hackathon Format</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Duration:</strong> 15 days from the official start of the hackathon.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Platform:</strong> This problem is hosted as a <strong>Kaggle competition</strong> with a live leaderboard.
      All scoring is based on submissions to Kaggle.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Submissions:</strong> You submit a <code>submission.csv</code> file to Kaggle. Each row contains
      an <code>image_id</code> and a corresponding path string (made of <code>l</code>, <code>r</code>, <code>u</code>,
      <code>d</code>) that describes how your agent moves from start to goal on that map.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Daily limit:</strong> Maximum <strong>5 submissions per day</strong> per team/account (Kaggle-enforced).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Leaderboard:</strong> Kaggle will show a public leaderboard during the competition. Final standings may use
      a hidden/private split of the test set.
    </li>
 <li>
      <strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> Ensure your Kaggle Username follows this exact format <code>NAME_ENROLMENTNO</code>. Any entries not following this format will be removed immediately!
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Deliverables</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>During the competition:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Upload <code>submission.csv</code> files to Kaggle and track your performance on the leaderboard.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>At the end of the competition:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Code Repository (GitHub):</strong> A public (or shareable) repo containing:
          <ul>
            <li>Training and inference code.</li>
            <li>Environment/requirements file.</li>
            <li>Instructions to reproduce your final submission.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Short Technical Report:</strong>
