10680,new-years-diet,"# Overview

Accurately estimating the nutritional content of meals from natural-language descriptions is a challenging and important task with applications in health, wellness, and food analytics. In this competition, participants are asked to predict key nutritional values based solely on a textual description of a meal.

Given a meal description, models must estimate four nutritional targets:

Calories (kilocalories)

Protein (grams)

Fat (grams)

Carbohydrates (grams)

The goal is to build models that can reason about food composition, portion size, and dietary context from unstructured text. Performance is evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE) averaged across the four targets.

This competition uses data  from the NutriBench dataset and is intended for non-commercial research and benchmarking purposes.
----------------------
# Description

This challenge is based on the [NutriBench](https://www.ai.ece.ucsb.edu/nutribench_v3) dataset. The goal of this challenge is to use the [Dowser](https://durinn-concept-explorer.azurewebsites.net/) research platform to find the best model and data to be most performant on this benchmark. 

This is a for fun challenge to help strengthen some cutting edge research. If you are interested in the tool being developed, please see the abstract below. 
[Dowser Abstract](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DVK1HS7N2Y3pAOMVbb7RCPPIjaONtzq4/view?usp=sharing)
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions in this competition are evaluated using **Mean Absolute Error (MAE)** across four nutritional targets.

For each meal description, participants must predict:

- Calories (kilocalories)
- Protein (grams)
- Fat (grams)
- Carbohydrates (grams)

This is a multi-output regression task.

---

## Evaluation Metric

The final score is calculated as the average Mean Absolute Error (MAE) across all four targets.

For each nutrient:
- The absolute difference between the predicted value and the true value is computed.
- These differences are averaged across all test samples to obtain the MAE for that nutrient.",,False,True
