10733,neural-machine-translator-deadline-extension,"# Overview

The goal will be to train a deep learning network to translate from French to English.

We will use a dataset of French-English pairs from the nonprofit Tatoeba.

1. Either use RNN only (LSTM or GRU)
2. Or RNN and an attention + RNN decoder
3. Or just attention (GPT)

One of 2. or 3. is necessary for this homework.
----------------------
# Description

You can get inspiration from [NLP from scratch PyTorch tutorial part 3](https://docs.pytorch.org/tutorials/intermediate/seq2seq_translation_tutorial.html).

Check the [Data](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/neural-machine-translator/data) tab for details.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Compute [BLEU score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BLEU) using torcheval's [bleu_score](https://meta-pytorch.org/torcheval/main/generated/torcheval.metrics.functional.bleu_score.html#torcheval.metrics.functional.bleu_score) with 4 n-grams.
    It is a weighted geometric mean of all the modified n-gram precisions, multiplied by the brevity penalty.

    >>> import pandas as pd
    >>> row_id_column_name = ""id""
    >>> y_pred = [""the squirrel is eating the nut"", ""the cat is on the mat""]
    >>> y_pred = pd.DataFrame(y_pred)
    >>> y_pred[""id""] = range(len(y_pred))
    >>> y_true = [""a squirrel is eating a nut|the squirrel is eating a tasty nut"", ""there is a cat on the mat|a cat is on the mat""]
    >>> y_true = pd.DataFrame(y_true)
    >>> y_true[""id""] = range(len(y_true))
    >>> score(y_true.copy(), y_pred.copy(), row_id_column_name)
    0.6534189

---

