**Meet the Avatars :** [Dr. Elena Vasquez](https://starshiptutor.substack.com/p/introducing-dr-elena-vasquez), [Evan Morales](https://starshiptutor.substack.com/p/introducing-evan-morales), [Maya Chen](https://starshiptutor.substack.com/p/introducing-maya-chen), [Daniel Reeve](https://starshiptutor.substack.com/p/introducing-daniel-reeve)<br>
**Kaggle Pages :** [Challenge 01](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/challenge-01-spaghetti-schema-2026), [Challenge 02](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/challenge-02-errors-integrity-2026), Challenge 03


You¡¯ll explore seasonal patterns, demand cycles, and external factors like pricing or holidays, turning raw transactions into predictive signals ready for strategy and simulation.
Your task is to build interpretable forecasting pipelines that are **transparent, reproducible, and business-aware** ¡ª where every chart and prediction can be traced back to trustworthy data.

This third milestone in the **Grocery Retail ¨C Driven by Data** series connects reliability with foresight.
You¡¯ll prove that clean data isn¡¯t just correct ¡ª it¡¯s *illuminating*.","# Dataset Description


# Data Dictionary ¡ª Challenge 3 Dataset

This dataset spans **2018¨C2022 (5 years)** of daily sales across 3 stores and 4 product categories.  
It is clean (no injected errors), designed for trend discovery, ARIMA/SARIMA forecasting,  
and unsupervised holiday/seasonality detection.


## stores.csv
| Column   | Type   | Description                | Example   |
|----------|--------|----------------------------|-----------|
| store_id | int    | Unique store identifier    | 1         |
| city     | string | City location of the store | Seattle   |
| size     | string | Store size category        | Large     |
| region   | string | Regional grouping          | NW        |


## categories.csv
| Column        | Type   | Description                                       | Example   |
|---------------|--------|---------------------------------------------------|-----------|
| category_id   | int    | Unique product category identifier                | 2         |
| name          | string | Category name                                     | Bakery    |
| seasonal_flag | int    | 1 = seasonal/holiday-driven, 0 = non-seasonal     | 1         |
| perishability | string | Perishability level                               | High      |


## dates.csv
| Column  | Type   | Description                        | Example   |
|---------|--------|------------------------------------|-----------|
| date    | date   | Calendar date                      | 2019-07-04 |
| dow     | int    | Day of week (0=Mon, 6=Sun)         | 3         |
| dom     | int    | Day of month                       | 4         |
| woy     | int    | ISO week of year                   | 27        |
| month   | int    | Month number (1¨C12)                | 7         |
| quarter | int    | Calendar quarter (1¨C4)             | 3         |
