10786,data-cleaning,"# Overview

Welcome to the Data Cleaning Challenge, a beginner-friendly data science competition focused on one of the most important (and overlooked) skills in real-world data science: cleaning messy data.

In this competition, you will receive a tabular dataset with realistic data quality issues such as missing values, inconsistent labels, corrupted numeric fields, and duplicate records. Your goal is to clean the data, prepare useful features, and build a model to make accurate predictions.

**Why This Competition?**
- In industry, most data science time is spent cleaning and preparing data. This challenge will help you:
- Practice identifying and fixing common data quality issues
- Build a reproducible data cleaning pipeline
- Understand how data quality affects model performance
- Gain experience with Kaggle-style workflows and submissions
----------------------
# Description

Real-world data is rarely clean. Before building models or drawing conclusions, data scientists spend a significant amount of time handling missing values, correcting inconsistencies, removing duplicates, and fixing corrupted entries. This competition is designed to help participants develop those foundational skills.

In this challenge, you will work with a messy tabular dataset that simulates common real-world data quality issues. Your goal is to clean the data and build a predictive model. Performance on the leaderboard will depend on how effectively you prepare the data and extract a meaningful signal.",,False,True
