----------------------
# Description

CodeFest is the annual technical festival of Computer Science and Engineering department at IIT BHU. Enigma has been a part of CodeFest since 2016. We aim to develop and nurture ML community and solve real world challenges. 

The problem statement for this challenge is brought to you by BondU Labs PVT LTD. 

The challenge for this year is to resolve the issue of participants of networking events to meet alike or complementary people who would be interested in collaboration or could benefit each other mutually. The goal of this competition is to build a model that can relate various attributes of one guest to other bidirectionally. **The dataset given to participants is generated mathematically and does not truly indicate the associativity of guests. Participants will not be judged solely on the basis of scores but also on the quality, idea and execution of the solution.**

We expect participants to not just develop a model with good scores but also a practical low to mid resource solution for enterprises and **not just a similarity model** but a solution with solid conceptual foundation. The final judgements will be made based on the practicality of the solution and not only the evaluation parameter.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Submissions will be evaluated using Mean Squared Error (MSE) between the predicted compatibility scores and the ground-truth compatibility values provided in `target.csv`.

Each row corresponds to a pair of participants, and the MSE is computed over all valid (`src_user_id`, `dst_user_id`) pairs. Lower MSE indicates better performance.

The evaluation encourages accurate and consistent estimation of pairwise compatibility scores across the entire participant set.

## Submission format

Participants must submit a CSV file containing pairwise compatibility predictions with the following columns:
```csv
src_user_id+'_'+dst_user_id, compatibility_score
```

## Format Details

- **`src_user_id:`** Profile ID of the source participant

- **`dst_user_id:`** Profile ID of the destination participant

- **`compatibility_score:`** Predicted compatibility score between the two participants

## Submission Constraints

- The submission must have same number of rows as the possible number of pairs in test data i.e. 16,000
- Ensure that all the entries are numbers and **headers are saved in csv file.**
- All the compatibility scores must be between 0 and 1.
- Ensure the ID row is string

## Sample submission
```csv
ID, compatibility_score
5601_5601,1
5601_5602,0.1538
5601_5603,0
5601_5604,0.2
```

## Leaderboard

* The **Public Leaderboard** reflects scores computed on the public portion of the validation data during the competition.
* Final rankings will be determined using a **Private Leaderboard**, evaluated on a hidden validation set.
* In case of a tie on the final leaderboard, the team with the **earlier valid submission** will be ranked higher.

