2. **Post-contrast T1-weighted (T1ce):** Highlights the ""Enhancing Tumor"" (active tumor cells).
3. **T2-weighted (T2):** Shows the outline of the brain and fluids.
4. **T2 Fluid Attenuated Inversion Recovery (FLAIR):** Critical for detecting ""Edema"" (swelling).

All files are in **NIfTI (.nii.gz)** format.",False,True
10799,cvpr-mslr-2026-track-2,"# Overview

> **Competition Dataset Released**  
> The dataset has been officially released and is now accessible to all participants.  
> You may start your experiments and submissions.  
> We look forward to your contributions and wish you the best of luck.

Welcome to the **2nd Multimodal Isolated Italian Sign Language (LIS) Recognition Challenge**.

Workshop site: [https://Multimodal-Sign-Language-Recognition.github.io/CVPR-2026/](https://Multimodal-Sign-Language-Recognition.github.io/CVPR-2026/)

This CVPR 2026 edition (Denver, **June 3 or 4, 2026**, TBD) asks you to build models that recognize **126 LIS gestures - 100 medical-domain words + 26 alphabet letters - using only Radar Time (RTM) data** captured with a 60 GHz sensor. The challenge uses **MultiMeDaLIS** range spectrum datas.

Top teams will be invited to present at the **MSLR Workshop @ CVPR 2026 in Denver (Colorado, USA)**, with certificates, and the opportunity to submit a challenge report paper.
----------------------
# Description

This edition is built around **MultiMeDaLIS**, a novel dataset that pairs visual and radar data to capture isolated Italian Sign Language gestures. Each of the 205 recorded sessions includes all 126 gesture classes, performed by a professional signer.

Important for this Kaggle track: the **leaderboard is Radar-Only**. You must use **RTM data**; RGB/RDM and others streams are **not** to be used for scoring.

**Why it¡¯s challenging**
- **Radar-only recognition**: no visual cues - learn micro-motion patterns from RTM
- **Realistic variation**: sensor viewpoint stress model robustness
- **Clinical vocabulary**: includes medical terms where subtle hand shapes and dynamics matter

**Data at a glance**
- 126 isolated LIS classes (100 medical + 26 letters)
- 60 GHz radar with L-shape antenna configuration (RTM provided)
- Multiple sessions per class

Bring your best representation learning, augmentation, and domain-robust strategies. Let¡¯s advance privacy-preserving, deployable sign recognition together - see you at CVPR in Denver!
----------------------
# Evaluation

Your submissions will be evaluated based on **Top-1 Accuracy** across the 126 gesture classes.

The competition includes:
- **Training Set**: 117 fully-labeled sessions
- **Validation Set**: 39 sessions without labels (for real-time leaderboard)
- **Test Set**: 39 sessions without labels (for final leaderboard)

You may submit **up to 2 predictions per day** on the validation leaderboard. Finalists must provide **code and model checkpoints** to ensure reproducibility.
----------------------
# Submission

Your submission should be a **CSV** file with the following format:
```python
id,Pred
0,23
1,78
¡­
```
- *id*: ID of each sample
- *Pred*: your predicted class ID for that sample (integer from 0 to 125)

Make sure your file includes **all samples** provided in the evaluation split. Only complete submissions will be scored.
----------------------
# Timeline (All deadlines are at 23:59 AoE)

- **Competition Launch & Training Data Release**: February 24, 2026
- **Validation Set Release**: February 24, 2026
- **Test Set Release**: March 10, 2026
- **Final Submission Deadline**: March 20, 2026
- **Invitation to publication Announced**: March 21, 2026
- **Paper Submission Deadline**: March 30, 2026
- **Workshop**: June 3-4, 2026 at CVPR 2026, Denver, Colorado
----------------------
