----------------------
# Description

![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-user-content/o/inbox%2F14564763%2F7127122281456a6570e1d17e1eace58d%2Fdunhuang.png?generation=1770047891983328&alt=media)

 Dynamic 3D Gaussian Splatting (DyGS) enables real-time, high-fidelity rendering of dynamic scenes and is increasingly used in AR/VR/XR and volumetric video. However, naively storing a time-varying set of Gaussian primitives leads to prohibitive storage and bandwidth costs. While many compression approaches have been proposed, progress is slowed by the lack of a standardized benchmark that evaluates rate, rendering quality, and online decoding cost under a unified protocol.

DyGS-Bench focuses on a realistic deployment setting where only the reconstructed native Gaussian sequence is available (no original multi-view training images/videos). The goal of this Grand Challenge is to advance practical codecs that compress dynamic Gaussian assets into a compact bitstream and reconstruct renderable Gaussians efficiently. 
----------------------
# Evaluation

<div align=""center"">

<h2>Image submission</h2>
<p align=""justify"">
For online testing convenience, this competition currently evaluates an <strong>image submission track</strong>:
participants upload their locally rendered test-view images. The scorer compares them against hidden GT images.
</p>

<h2>Metrics</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>PSNR</strong> (higher is better)</li>
  <li><strong>SSIM</strong> (higher is better)</li>
  <li><strong>Size</strong> (lower is better)</li>
  <li><strong>tOF</strong> (lower is better)</li>
</ul>
  <h3>Definitions</h3>


  <h4>PSNR</h4>
  <p>
    \( \mathrm{MSE}=\frac{1}{3HW}\sum_{c=1}^{3}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{w=1}^{W}\big(\hat I_{c,h,w}-I_{c,h,w}\big)^2 \)
  </p>
  <p>
    \( \mathrm{PSNR}=10\log_{10}\left(\frac{1}{\mathrm{MSE}}\right) \)
  </p>

  <h4>SSIM</h4>
  <p>
    \( \mathrm{SSIM}(x,y)=\frac{(2\mu_x\mu_y+C_1)(2\sigma_{xy}+C_2)}{(\mu_x^2+\mu_y^2+C_1)(\sigma_x^2+\sigma_y^2+C_2)} \)
  </p>


  <h4>tOF (TecoGAN)</h4>
  <p>
    \( F^{GT}_t=\mathrm{OF}(I_{t-1},I_t),\quad F^{Pred}_t=\mathrm{OF}(\hat I_{t-1},\hat I_t) \)
  </p>
  <p>
    \( \mathrm{tOF}=\frac{1}{T-1}\sum_{t=2}^{T}\left(\frac{1}{HW}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{w=1}^{W}\left\|F^{Pred}_t(h,w)-F^{GT}_t(h,w)\right\|_{1}\right) \)
  </p>

<h2>Submission Package (template)</h2>
<p align=""justify"">Unless otherwise stated, please prepare a single zip file with the following structure:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;scene_name&gt;/
  frame000000/
      cam00.png
      cam01.png
      ...
  frame000001/
      cam00.png
    ...

</code></pre>
<p align=""justify"">
<strong>Note:</strong> Your submission must contain the required images for each GT frame/camera you want to be evaluated on.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>For questions about evaluation rules or submission formatting, please contact the organizers listed on the Organizers page.</p>","# Dataset Description

<div align=""center"">


<h2>Data Access</h2>
<p align=""justify""><strong>By accessing the data, participants agree to the dataset license and the challenge Terms &amp; Conditions.</strong></p>

<h2>Dataset: Native Dynamic Gaussian Sequences</h2>
<p align=""justify"">
DyGS-Bench focuses on a <strong>native Gaussians-only</strong> setting: the input is a reconstructed dynamic 3D Gaussian sequence (no original multi-view training RGB/video data). Each sequence includes:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Native Gaussian assets</strong>: time-varying Gaussians (per-frame PLY).</li>
  <li><strong>Camera set</strong>: calibrated camera parameters for rendering-based evaluation.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Download</h2>
<p align=""justify"">
The dataset is hosted on HuggingFace:
<a href=""https://huggingface.co/datasets/LeeXiangNO1/DyNativeGaussian_sequence"" target=""_blank"">
https://huggingface.co/datasets/LeeXiangNO1/DyNativeGaussian_sequence
</a>
</p>

<h2>Recommended Local Folder Structure (example)</h2>
<pre><code>DyNativeGaussian_sequence/
  &lt;scene_name&gt;/
    sparse/
      camera.txt
    gaussians/
      000000.ply
      000001.ply
      ...
        ...
</code></pre>

<h2>Stage</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Stage One</strong>:We will release part of the dataset for training and testing your method. Among the camera viewpoints we provide, two are designated as test viewpoints for platform evaluation. We recommend not attempting to perform supervised training on the test viewpoints, as it is meaningless to boost rankings in the first stage. In the second stage, source code submission will be required, and at that time, the test viewpoints provided by us will not belong to any known subset.</li>
  <li><strong>Stage Two</strong>: We will provide additional data sets, as well as notebooks with source code and decoding templates. Please create your own decoding scripts based on these templates. In phase two, you need to provide encoded files and decoding scripts for each data set. We will test the effectiveness of the method on the platform.</li>

</ul>

<h2>Citation</h2>
<p align=""justify"">
If you use the dataset and benchmark in a publication, please cite the DyGS-Bench paper (citation will be updated here once the preprint is public).
</p>",False,True
