# Rules & Guidelines 

## 1. Data & Model Usage

- External data is strictly prohibited.
- The use of proprietary, paid, or closed-source models is strictly forbidden.
- Foundation Models & VLMs: The use of Large Language Models (LLMs) or Vision-Language Models (VLMs) for finetuning, labeling, classification, or inference is strictly prohibited and will result in disqualification.
- Object Detection Foundation Models: The use of foundation models for object detection or segmentation (e.g., SAM, Grounding DINO, or similar zero-shot architectures) is strictly forbidden.

## 2. Code Submission & Reproducibility

- Participants who finish in the Top 10 on the Private Leaderboard are required to publicly share their full training and inference code, and ensure it can reproduce the final score.
- The code must be published within a maximum of two (2) days after the competition ends; otherwise, the participant may be removed from the leaderboard.
- Teams are encouraged to publish a short article or blog explaining the model selection, design decisions, and training strategy.

## 3. Participation Rules

- Participation is individually, or in teams of up to three (3) members.
- Participation certificates will be provided.
- The use of duplicate or multiple accounts is strictly prohibited and will result in immediate disqualification.

## 4. Prize Eligibility

- Monetary prizes are limited to participants residing in Saudi Arabia.
- Non-residents are welcome to participate but are not eligible for monetary prizes.

