10810,sh4rlocked,"# Overview

The London Fog & The Dying Light: A Denoising Challenge
The game is afoot, and the stakes couldn't be higher.

Our world was once illuminated by a constant, unwavering light a pristine dataset of ten distinct classes, guarded by a master of deduction: the CNN Guardian. But a dense, unnatural fog has rolled in. Every image is now shrouded in noise, obscuring the ""clues"" the Guardian needs to make its judgment. As the light of the original signal fades, we face a total blackout of information.

Your task is to step into the role of the consulting chemist. You must synthesize a denoising mechanism to peel back the layers of corruption and reveal the truth hidden beneath. We aren't looking to train a new detective; we are looking to clear the air so the one we have can see again.

The Case File
The Guardian's vision is failing. It was trained on the clarity of the ""old world,"" and it refuses to adapt to the new, distorted reality. To save the signal, you must focus on the data itself.

The Victim: A dataset of 10 image classes, currently buried under a ""smog"" of Gaussian and salt-and-pepper noise.

The Witness: A Pretrained CNN Classifier. Its weights are frozen. It is a brilliant but stubborn mind it will only provide the correct answer if you give it a clear picture.

The Mission: Reconstruct the signal. You must develop a model perhaps a Convolutional Autoencoder or a U-Net architecture that can act as a lens, filtering out the chaos before it reaches the Guardian.
----------------------
# Evaluation

Your success depends entirely on how clearly the Detective can see through your restored images.

Evaluation Metric: The primary score is the Classification Accuracy of the Pretrained Guardian CNN¡¯s predictions on the hidden test set.

The Mission: Your goal is to maximize this accuracy by providing the cleanest possible data to the frozen model.

The Submission Protocol
To close the case, you must transmit your findings in a specific format. Each ""reality"" you restore must be reported with its true identity and the Detective's final classification.

The ID: This represents the filename of the image. (e.g., if the processed image is 12345.jpg, the ID must be 12345).

The Label: This is the integer class predicted by the Guardian CNN after your denoising magic has been applied.

Note: The Detective's logic is immutable. Do not attempt to alter his mind (the CNN weights). Focus solely on the clarity of the evidence you provide.
Your final submission file should be a CSV formatted as follows:ID,Label
10001,3
10002,0
10003,9","# Dataset Description

The Smog of London & The Dying Sun: The Restoration Mission
The game is afoot, but the streets of London are no longer visible. A thick, synthetic smog a ""digital fog"" has rolled in, obscuring the truth and dimming the light of our civilization. The sun is cooling, and we have only a limited window to restart the core of our data before the freeze becomes permanent.

This competition provides a synthetic grayscale image dataset, forged to test your forensic ability. You must peel back the layers of corruption and reclaim clarity all without altering the mind of the Great Detective (the Guardian CNN).

 The Baker Street Archives: Shrouded Evidence
In the aftermath of the ""Great Obscuration,"" the once-clear images of our world have fractured. What remains are grayscale fragments scattered across ten distinct categories of evidence. The original, pure records are lost... but their essence lingers in the shadows, waiting for a mind sharp enough to see them.

Every image you receive has been tainted by structured noise, clouding the Guardian¡¯s perception and rendering its once-perfect deductions useless.

The Contents of the Archive

train_noisy/ ¡ª The Fog-Bound Streets: These are the corrupted training images¡ªechoes of the original evidence. Use these to experiment and refine your denoising ""chemicals."" While the clean versions are absent, the Guardian can still sense fragments of truth. Use its feedback to measure how close your restoration brings you to the light.

test_noisy/ ¡ª The Final Eight Minutes: Once your denoising process is perfected, this is where you prove your mastery. Each image here is part of the hidden case file unseen, unlabeled, and waiting for the light. Your final pipeline must operate here to produce the Detective¡¯s ultimate verdict before the sun goes dark.

 The Guardian and Its Instruments
The Detective does not change his mind to fit the world; he expects the world to be presented clearly so he can deduce the truth.

model.pth - The Guardian CNN: Trained long ago when the sun was bright and the air was clear. Its knowledge is ancient and immutable. You cannot retrain or fine-tune it. Your task is to restore its vision, not its memory.

model.py - The Architect¡¯s Blueprint: A map of the Guardian¡¯s mental structure. Use it to summon and load the model correctly into your computational workspace.

The Final Deduction
""We are all just stardust, waiting for the fog to clear.""

The original world is gone, but the shadows remain. Your mission is to bring them back into focus, clear the smog from the streets, and restart the heart of the Data-Verse. If you fail to remove the noise, the Detective remains blind, and the light fails for us all.

Eliminate the impossible. Restore the signal.",False,True
