10816,dartmouth-cosc-74-w26-competition-02,"# Overview

Your objective is to construct action recognition models on a subset of [the UCF101 dataset](https://www.crcv.ucf.edu/data/UCF101.php). The UCF101 dataset consists of a total of 13,320 videos spanning diverse human action categories. However, for the final project, our focus narrows down to a subset of the dataset, comprising 2,355 training videos and 969 test videos distributed among 30 action categories. You will have to build one binary classifier and one multi-class classifier.

In this competition, your task is to build a multi-class classifier for all 30 action classes. Your goal is to train a model to classify videos into corresponding categories. You are free to choose any machine learning models from the class.

For more details regarding the tasks, including the dataset download, please refer to the information provided in [this Google Colab link](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1dazZqyBdniYmKDtMPypl0aDfOgZF_67l?usp=sharing).

Please note that **the deadline for project submission is Monday, March 09, 11:59 pm**. 
----------------------
# Evaluation

The evaluation metric for this competition is **Accuracy**.","# Dataset Description

For more details regarding the tasks, including the dataset download, please refer to the information provided in [this Google Colab link](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/19IOk0hmokk726V2WRwNsX9TQDlcRECuU?usp=sharing).",False,True
10817,dartmouth-cosc-74-w26-competition-01,"# Overview

Your objective is to construct action recognition models on a subset of [the UCF101 dataset](https://www.crcv.ucf.edu/data/UCF101.php). The UCF101 dataset consists of a total of 13,320 videos spanning diverse human action categories. However, for the final project, our focus narrows down to a subset of the dataset, comprising 2,355 training videos and 969 test videos distributed among 30 action categories. You will have to build one binary classifier and one multi-class classifier.

In this competition, your task is to build a classifier for the class *JugglingBalls*. Your goal is to train a model to classify JugglingBalls videos as *positive* and the remaining videos as *negative*. You are free to choose any machine learning models from the class. 

For more details regarding the tasks, including the dataset download, please refer to the information provided in [this Google Colab link](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1dazZqyBdniYmKDtMPypl0aDfOgZF_67l?usp=sharing).

