Public project link (if applicable)

?? Evaluation Criteria

Submissions will be judged based on:

Innovation & originality

Technical implementation quality

Real-world usefulness and impact

Clarity and completeness of documentation

?? Who Should Participate

This hackathon welcomes:

Data scientists & AI engineers

Behavioral researchers & psychologists

Crisis management professionals

Students and innovators

Anyone interested in human intelligence & decision science

? Ethical Considerations

Solutions should promote responsible AI use, respect privacy, and avoid harmful or discriminatory outcomes.
----------------------
# Submission Requirements

? Submission Requirements

A valid submission must include the following components. Submissions that do not meet these requirements may not be evaluated.

Your final submission must be submitted before the competition deadline. Draft or unsubmitted Writeups will not be reviewed by the judges.

To submit your project, create a Writeup and click the Submit button after saving.

?? Note: If you attach a private Kaggle resource to your Writeup, it will automatically become public after the submission deadline.

1?? Kaggle Writeup (Required)

The Kaggle Writeup serves as the official project report and must include:

Project Title & Subtitle

Problem statement and motivation

Methodology and approach

Results and insights

Real-world use case or impact

Limitations and future improvements

