?? 6. Also submit your predictions CSV file

7. Don't forget to also complete? [Homework 5: Conceptual](https://www.gradescope.com/courses/1059155/assignments/6459799)

  

  

  

  

## Submitting Predictions to Kaggle

  

Your starter notebook contains code that outputs predictions into a file called `submission.csv`. See instructions and screenshots in that file for submitting to Kaggle. This file only needs the `userid_DI` and `certified` columns to compare to the true answers in order to evaluate your model. For example, the following is valid output (only the first row is shown):

  

```

userid_DI, certified

MHxPC130476531, 0

...

```

  

To simplify getting the Kaggle format right, we have provided a code snippet that you should use to save the Kaggle submission. This code is already included in the starter code.

  

```

df_test = pd.read_csv('edx_test.csv')

  

# Any code to pre-process the data?

...

  

